          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared font-index directory permits staging symlink overwrites\n\nNative font-index saving writes to a predictable PID-based temporary file with fs::write. If an operator places the index in a directory writable by a less-trusted local user, that user can redirect a cache save to another victim-writable file.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Symlink following in font cache publication\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-59, CWE-377, CWE-61\n\nRemediation:\nPublish the font index through an unpredictable private staging directory and an exclusively created regular file held open through writing. Atomically rename only that file; refuse preexisting staging entries and document/private-parent expectations for shared configurations.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A planted temporary symlink must be refused without changing its referent.\n- Concurrent cache saves and collisions preserve a complete regular index.\n- Disabled cache and default private-directory lookup keep working.\n- Integration-test a preplanted PID temporary symlink under a configured shared cache and verify referent preservation.\n- Verify disabled index and private normal cache paths retain intended behavior.\n- Filesystem integration test with a link at the legacy PID temporary path leaves its referent unchanged.\n- Concurrent index writers use independent exclusive staging files."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:897bff81ebad60d9ef8c3f51f73cda8028de4287ad6fdf7cc9641a48dd0caba6"
          },
