          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Converting cyclic Markdown drawing payloads can terminate the host process\n\nAn attacker-supplied Markdown image with a `drawing:` payload can encode a dependency pointing back to itself. `markdown_to_docx` accepts the flat JSON graph and recursively materializes it without cycle detection, exhausting the stack or memory before conversion returns.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled recursion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nValidate drawing dependency graphs before materialization. Reject cycles and excessive traversal depth/work, and memoize materialized indexes so shared dependencies are not repeatedly expanded.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Assert self cycles and two-node cycles return structured errors without recursion.\n- Assert deeply nested and exponentially shared acyclic graphs obey an explicit work budget.\n- Preserve valid shared dependency round trips."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:9e50345c635c39a9aed6ac0ea98a66d37c5e1123e1493206787371c747b396a6"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled recursion",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_d84eab4d13fbce226cc028c6",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_01323297e0fd75cfe9967c93",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "uncontrolled-recursion.drawing-dependencies",
          "ruleIndex": 70
        },
