          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Metadata scrub leaves property parts under alternate names\n\nWith docprops enabled, scrub removes metadata only from three conventional filenames. A document using alternate package relationship targets can retain creators, editors, dates, company/manager or custom properties while scrub returns success. The custom-properties branch additionally skips relationship/content-type removal when docProps/custom.xml is absent, leaving an active relationship to a relocated target such as metadata/private.xml.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Incomplete removal of sensitive document metadata Incomplete removal of sensitive metadata Incomplete privacy sanitization Incomplete metadata selection for privacy removal\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-212, CWE-201, CWE-200\n\nRemediation:\nResolve all core, extended and custom property parts through authoritative package relationships and content types, sanitize every applicable internal target according to docprops selection, and remove corresponding custom-property parts/relationships/content-type records coherently. Verify the selected privacy postcondition; refuse unsupported or ambiguous layouts rather than returning a successfully scrubbed copy. Preserve intentional title/subject/application and revision-date retention. Missing/invalid selected targets require explicit refusal or documented safe handling; default public and CLI callers must enforce the same postcondition. Include supported Strict property relationship variants and regression cases containing both conventional and relocated targets; every active property target must satisfy the requested postcondition.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Use alternate core/app/custom filenames and case variants with valid relationships/content types.\n- Confirm selected fields/parts are absent and references coherent afterward.\n- Keep intentional title/subject/application retention.\n- Integration tests relocate each metadata part and update its relationship/content type, then verify the same fields are removed from outgoing package bytes.\n- Cover multiple metadata relationships and conventional paths without losing unrelated intentional content.\n- Relocate core/extended/custom parts with corresponding relationships and assert default scrub removes identifying values.\n- Scrub core, extended and custom properties at relocated relationship-selected targets and assert requested identities are absent.\n- Cover conventional paths, multiple metadata relationships and missing/invalid targets with explicit refusals or documented handling.\n- Relocate each supported document-property part and relationship and assert docprops removes the selected metadata.\n- Verify no stale custom-properties relationship or content-type override remains.\n- Scrub core/app/custom metadata at alternate relationship targets and require equivalent removal.\n- Cover multiple metadata targets and conventional-path decoys.\n- Relocate each property class independently with matching relationship/content type and verify requested fields or entire custom part are absent.\n- Cover packages with both conventional and relocated targets and verify no active property target survives unexpectedly.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Drive semantic metadata removal from OPC relationships/content types rather than conventional filenames."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:01549dc965ee1982345ae47c1492f7931844bc5e65ba231ca9c5c89fba11be2d"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Incomplete removal of sensitive document metadata\nIncomplete removal of sensitive metadata\nIncomplete privacy sanitization\nIncomplete metadata selection for privacy removal",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_4b64ae60e06cc87420036fe5",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_036ee756df4ef46be74a8ef2",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "metadata-scrub.relationship-targets",
          "ruleIndex": 27
        },
