          "message": {
            "text": "Redacting text can leave recoverable copies in UTF-16 XML\n\nA successful redact edit can retain the same secret in a UTF-16 `customXml` part. Admission accepts that encoding, but the final leak check treats XML as UTF-8 and misses the duplicate before returning the clean DOCX.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Incomplete sensitive data redaction\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-200\n\nRemediation:\nShare the XML decoder used by admission with the leak scanner, decode UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE before xml_holds, and refuse unrecognized/invalid encodings rather than silently classifying them as clean. Preserve raw-byte checks as defense in depth. Add redaction tests proving a UTF-16 customXml duplicate causes REDACTION_LEAK and no artifact is returned.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Redact a UTF-8 paragraph with UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE customXml duplicates and require REDACTION_LEAK.\n- Exercise unsupported or invalid XML encodings and ensure the checker fails closed."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:0aaa2bcb9fc426902b81c4cf21234bba88d7870e93e31afbdc8d8339b581982e"
          },
