          "message": {
            "text": "Listing many comments over one large range multiplies retained anchor text\n\nA document with many comments covering the same large text range is small relative to the comment listing it produces. list_comments copies the full range into every CommentRecord without an expanded-output budget, allowing a compact document to demand gigabytes of retained memory.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Allocation without resource limits\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-770\n\nRemediation:\nEnforce a cumulative comment-anchor/output byte budget before cloning, return a typed refusal or bounded/truncated representation, and consider shared ranges or streaming records instead of duplicating every full anchor in memory.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Many comments sharing a large range must stop at a deterministic output budget.\n- Small overlapping comments should retain accurate anchor/context data."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:fef3817c751a47713a38a1fbf2661a476da31e9d9c3c2de078749abe71e374f5"
