          "message": {
            "text": "Repeated relationship IDs trigger quadratic repair work\n\nOpening a package repairs identical duplicate relationship IDs. For n distinct IDs each repeated identically, each repair linearly searches an increasingly long Vec, producing quadratic CPU work on shallow metadata that fits existing byte and attribute limits.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nTrack already-reported duplicate IDs in a HashSet or alongside seen-map state, retaining a Vec only for deterministic reporting order. Optionally cap relationship-record/work totals before repair; test many distinct identical duplicate pairs while preserving deterministic repaired-ID order and conflicting-duplicate refusals.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Use a deterministic operation-count/scaling test with many distinct identical duplicate pairs.\n- Retain behavior tests for conflicting duplicates and deterministic repaired-ID order at both package and part level.\n- Use operation counters to verify linear repair for many IDs each repeated twice.\n- Preserve identical-duplicate reporting order and refusal of conflicting duplicates.\n- Many distinct IDs each repeated twice must preserve first records and report each repair once with work scaling linearly.\n- Conflicting duplicates must still be refused.\n- Exercise many distinct identical duplicates and assert membership work stays linear.\n- Retain conflicting-duplicate refusal and deterministic repair order."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:1bd7b31cd0a1107bff1f4297105e24d5c943ff9c4ddbdf12d64bd87007090e7a"
          },
