          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Redacting a numeric identifier can leave its custom XML attribute intact\n\nThe final redaction leak scan exempts numeric-looking attributes by local name alone. A sensitive value such as a customer or account identifier in custom XML `id` is ignored, allowing visible redaction to succeed while the value remains recoverable in the returned DOCX.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Overbroad sensitive data scan exemption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-201, CWE-200\n\nRemediation:\nRemove numeric exemptions from strict redaction verification, or restrict them to verified OOXML namespace/element/attribute combinations representing exclusively generated layout state. Always scan arbitrary custom XML business attributes.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Redact visible numeric targets duplicated in unqualified and business-namespaced custom XML id attributes; assert REDACTION_LEAK.\n- Retain explicit tests for legitimate OOXML layout exemptions only if their exact namespace and element contexts are enforced.\n- Redact an account identifier also held by customXml metadata/@id and assert refusal.\n- Keep regression coverage for legitimate qualified OOXML numeric layout attributes and scan the same local names in unrelated namespaces."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:ada4a4393ae672971fa6e00d68ec5f599fa6d53e35f71db2144f50efd12e7e6a"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Overbroad sensitive-data scan exemption",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_e317a396f5a5264629caef58",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_1afa7106488aceef728fbfdb",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "redaction-verification.namespace-blind-attributes",
          "ruleIndex": 35
        },
