          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering nested HTML tables bypasses the XML depth limit\n\nHTML table expansion runs after package admission and can generate arbitrarily deep WordprocessingML, which is passed to the unchecked recursive DOM parser. The supplied corroboration preserves the innermost-paragraph prerequisite for retaining nested cell WML and confirms that huge colspan is unnecessary; exact abort depth is platform-dependent.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nBound HTML nesting/generated output and validate expanded WML under active depth/tag limits before DOM construction.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Deep nested HTML refuses before recursive DOM parsing.\n- Bounded nested tables continue to render correctly.\n- Refuse deeply nested HTML altChunks before recursive DOM construction.\n- Accept nested HTML tables within the active XML-depth budget and retain their content."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:c4770cdf706671a451b4c46508dcc77e5871ce94631bba37ce33b6cbf275c383"
          },
