          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded tab-leader positions create attacker-sized repeated strings\n\nA very large left tab stop with a dot, hyphen or underscore leader makes document rendering allocate and shape a huge repeated string, even when the stop lies far outside the page.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Memory allocation with excessive size value\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nReject nonfinite coordinates and cap tab destinations or generated leader glyphs to the visible line/page extent before constructing strings.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Bound huge finite and nonfinite Left/Center/Decimal/Right tab positions before repeated string construction.\n- Exercise dot, hyphen and underscore leaders across compatibility modes and small font widths.\n- Huge finite, nonfinite and negative tab positions return a typed refusal or bounded rendering.\n- Exercise left/center/decimal and legacy right tabs; downstream raster limits must not be the first guard.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Bound derived dimensions and generated output independently from archive/XML input byte limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:dc42c3289f16b0c4ef06bc55a7f252e3d027af70111f7d8b31b4217548a19567"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Memory allocation with excessive size value",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_f23ce2ece7c2d5de613bb58d",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_1e5fd4df79504f20452df44e",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "unbounded-allocation.tab-leader",
          "ruleIndex": 58
        },
