          "message": {
            "text": "Comparing large tables can allocate a quadratic matrix\n\nTable alignment allocates an unchecked (old_rows+1) by (new_rows+1) usize matrix. A few-megabyte pair of 20,000-row tables can request about 3.2 GB before output.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nCheck row products against a comparison work/memory budget before all nested scans/allocations and use bounded-memory alignment or a typed refusal for excessive work.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Large unmerged changed tables refuse or use bounded-memory alignment before matrix allocation.\n- Apply the same budget to shared-word and content row LCS."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:f1d6a1e76609fb8535cbda6b04c50b4ebb5bc6cc1c0cec7491dd42240d890f68"
