            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Python CLI output/plan and npm direct-output symlinks can overwrite unrelated files\n\nPython and npm ordinary-output helpers check pathname existence separately from truncating writes; a local writer of the selected directory can replace an output name and redirect generated bytes to a victim-writable file. Python plan recording additionally uses a predictable basename/PID partial pathname without exclusive creation. The assigned report also corroborates npm plan staging, which is represented by the separately retained symlink-following.plan-staging finding. Without --force, a stable symlink to an existing referent is refused; post-preflight substitution bypasses that refusal, and a dangling link can pass the existence test. Filesystem/OS protections and shared-directory authority remain prerequisites. The shared writers also publish read/compare/revision results, document/PDF/PNG and font/render products, edit/visual-diff bundles, field-update reports, and repair outputs.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-61, CWE-367\n\nRemediation:\nPublish Python/Node ordinary outputs, bundles and reports through held-directory authority and exclusive private staging. Atomically install without replacement when --force is false, or atomically replace the authorized destination entry when true; never truncate through a mutable final pathname. Apply exclusive unpredictable regular-file staging beside the authorized target to Python plan recording. Node recordPlan staging retains its separately established repair and identity.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Integration: preplant a symlink at the plan partial path and assert its referent remains unchanged.\n- Integration: replace an output between preflight and publication and assert no unrelated referent is modified.\n- Verify atomic no-clobber and existing/dangling symlink handling for ordinary outputs, reports and edit bundles in both CLI adapters.\n- Integration-test destination substitution between preflight and commit for both adapters and verify outside referents remain unchanged.\n- Test dangling symlinks, newly occupied outputs, and authorized --force replacement.\n- Insert a destination between preflight and publication and verify no-force refuses it without changing its referent.\n- Cover all side products and verify --force replaces only the selected directory entry rather than following a substituted link.\n- Insert an output symlink between preflight and commit; verify no-force refuses it and preserves the referent.\n- Verify forced publication replaces the entry without modifying its symlink referent.\n- Apply checks to PDF/PNG, edited outputs, read exports, comparison and report publication.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce overwrite policy at the commit operation, never only at a prior existence check."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:cd37474aab446b5dcff390ae52cccb92a8c24fa43294cf860648eaee371bdbfc"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unsafe filesystem publication / symbolic link following",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_1bcd308b4a2806997600d807",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_216b2e0b08f7fa7579e809bd",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "unsafe-filesystem-publication.symlink-following",
          "ruleIndex": 77
        },
