          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Attacker-controlled list levels cause billions of iterations and counter allocations\n\nDOCX paragraph, style, and numbering definitions accept arbitrary u32 list levels. An undefined level near u32::MAX drives a descending search through billions of integers; defining that level instead makes next_marker create a counter for every lower level. A tiny document can monopolize CPU or exhaust memory during rendering.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unchecked input controlling resource consuming loops\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-606\n\nRemediation:\nValidate paragraph, style, abstract-level and override ilvl values against the supported numbering-level range before storing or using them. Iterate only bounded known levels for lookup, counters and placeholders; reject unsupported values with a typed error.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Add deterministic bounded tests for ilvl at the last supported value and just outside it, plus u32::MAX-1.\n- Exercise undefined high-level lookup and explicitly defined high-level counters; assert prompt refusal without iterating the numeric range."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:5d912eb35ec75f600afac931a891f445b5456cbfb242f6b00290562e79e5a53f"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unchecked input controlling resource-consuming loops",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_e3e47288f289bb478cceac76",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_2e5ab30849f2de8a853351e4",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "unbounded-numbering-level-iteration",
          "ruleIndex": 67
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
