          "message": {
            "text": "Inspecting many alternating-format runs repeatedly scans the whole paragraph prefix\n\nA document author can place many short runs with alternating formatting in a single paragraph. The inspector repeatedly counts characters from the paragraph start for every span boundary, causing quadratic CPU work in public inspection and downstream editing views.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nConvert sorted byte boundaries to character offsets in one forward pass, or construct a byte-to-character index once, then look up every span boundary.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Use a deterministic character-visit counter for a long alternating-format paragraph and assert linear work.\n- Preserve Unicode byte-to-character correctness and adjacent-format merging."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:ebbf9f0548767c78688bbe82dee7c25e75e02cb63b8b3b5e523a5e78c75ddbce"
          },
          "properties": {
