          "message": {
            "text": "npm CLI output writes follow substituted symlinks\n\nThe npm CLI checks existsSync separately from default fs.writeFileSync. A local actor controlling output directory entries can substitute a link to a victim-writable file; the generated document/report write then truncates the referent. Dangling output symlinks bypass the no-force existence check.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Check then write symlink race\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-367\n\nRemediation:\nUse exclusive no-clobber creation for absent outputs and private staging with atomic rename when replacement is authorized. Hold the destination parent and avoid reopening a checked final path with symlink-following truncation.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A pre-placed staging/output symlink never changes its referent.\n- A destination created after a no-force check is refused atomically; authorized replacement installs at the selected entry.\n- Verify final-path and parent-substitution behavior on supported platforms."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:07342eb0e44ddddf865da794ff2666554c923b971ec727b766c70767e7dd9372"
          },
