          "message": {
            "text": "Redaction postcondition misses confidential phrases split across DrawingML runs\n\nThe final leak check joins WordprocessingML run text but checks DrawingML chart text only one node at a time. A phrase split between adjacent chart-title runs survives a successful body redaction and remains recoverable from both output packages. The corroborating source includes preserved chart/diagram DrawingML a:p/a:r/a:t subpaths and downstream Office rendering; disclosure still requires sharing the result.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Incomplete removal of sensitive information during redaction\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-212\n\nRemediation:\nExtend leak detection to logical text of supported components, including DrawingML paragraphs/chart rich text, aligning with extraction logic. Add a body-redaction regression with matching split chart-title text and require refusal for both output packages. Include preserved diagram paragraphs as well as chart-title rich text, and fail closed when a supported text-bearing structure cannot be inspected.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Package regression with a body redaction and the same secret split across a:p/a:r/a:t in a preserved chart or diagram; require REDACTION_LEAK."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:59c0bb918748e464543916a4566c372e5de59b54c3b865e3eab7b394f3238e0f"
