          "message": {
            "text": "Streaming XML hash repeatedly rescans growing escaped opening tags\n\nHashXmlBuf searches the entire accumulated opening tag for > after every emitted fragment. Escaped attribute values emit one fragment per character; retained custom-namespace paragraph attributes select this fallback hashing path, causing quadratic CPU consumption within admitted XML sizes.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity in XML hashing\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nSearch only the new fragment for the root-tag terminator or expose explicit tag-completion state from serialization. Preserve linear behavior for escaped values and test large retained custom attributes through public comparison.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Compare genuinely differing in-memory documents with a large allowed custom-namespace paragraph attribute containing many escaped characters; assert bounded work without repeated scans of accumulated opening-tag bytes.\n- Retain correct hashes for ordinary attributes and for the custom-namespace fallback, including fragments that terminate or span the root opening tag."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:fd01e0a2f47f92980d7b3d986e91612dc5725a0fe0b981de176251b240b0d113"
