          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering a DOCX with renamed auxiliary XML can exhaust the call stack\n\nA DOCX styles, theme or font-table relationship can target a deeply nested part named `.bin`. Admission skips its XML limits, but rendering parses it recursively and can abort the conversion process.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: XML resource limit bypass\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nBefore each renderer DOM construction, use try_parse_xdocument_with_limits with the active limits, or admit all relationship/content-type identified XML parts regardless of filename suffix. Add integration regressions for over-depth styles/theme parts named .bin and verify the ordinary INVALID_XML refusal on PDF and PNG paths.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Render over-depth styles/theme/fontTable XML with .bin names and expect INVALID_XML for PDF and PNG.\n- Confirm ordinary admitted relationship targets still render."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:c59d58d06fdd105ce894e08d6df006da724ca6ca2fba8f5130a708258ee12895"
