          "message": {
            "text": "Report text extraction quadratically groups baselines on tall pages\n\npage_text searches the entire existing-baseline Vec for every text op, while document-controlled page height permits arbitrarily many distinct baselines on a single page. 100000 distinct one-character baselines cause about5billion key comparisons. A report-only request does not pass through MAX_PAGE_PIXELS destination allocation checks.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Quadratic rendered text grouping\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nIndex baseline keys with a HashMap or BTreeMap while retaining first-seen output order; enforce aggregate text-operation/work limits independently of raster page-size limits.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Report-only extraction with many distinct baselines must have near-linear key lookup work independent of page geometry."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
