          "message": {
            "text": "Revision settlement performs quadratic paragraph correspondence work\n\nA compact DOCX with many paragraphs and one tracked insertion can force a Cartesian scan of original and settled paragraphs when an ordinary edit/read/template request accepts or rejects revisions. The scan runs even when no paragraph merged, allowing disproportionate CPU use.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Inefficient algorithmic complexity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nBuild merged-member counts and singleton source indexes in one pass over fates, keyed by settled paragraph, then inspect only singleton merged groups. Review neighboring repeated scans and enforce an explicit correspondence-work budget.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Exercise many unchanged paragraphs plus one settled run revision and assert correspondence work remains linear.\n- Cover v1/v2, read-for-edit and template consumers while retaining merged-singleton correctness."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
