          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Markdown reference DOCX reaches recursive XML parsing before admission\n\nMarkdown-to-DOCX reference bytes are opened with the bounded OPC loader but are not XML-admitted before frame/final_section parses the main XML recursively. A deeply nested reference can exhaust a native stack or trap WASM before the configured depth refusal.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nAdmit the reference before any consumed part reaches the permissive parser, or use checked parsing with explicit limits for every consumed reference XML part.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A bounded regression for the identified input returns a normal refusal or bounded result before large allocation/recursion.\n- Ordinary documents at the active boundary continue to parse under caller-selected limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:066f43bbb1f5f7a575b333d7f1f77ad9e7fc30a0b517254fb8252575e196541a"
