          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Processing renamed auxiliary XML bypasses XML depth limits\n\nA DOCX author can put deeply nested auxiliary XML under a non-.xml/.rels suffix. Admission drains those bytes without XML policy, while rendering, revision listing, revision acceptance/rejection and comparison follow internal relationships and recursively build a DOM. Confirmed rendering parts include theme, styles, numbering, comments/commentsExtended, notes and headers/footers; get_revisions and comparison also parse renamed footnotes/endnotes. A small admitted package can terminate the native host or trap WASM. The assigned source additionally confirms eager relationship-selected fontTable parsing before font inspection, including renamed fontTable.bin. Comparison preprocessing also follows renamed styles and charts, alongside footnotes/endnotes. The assigned Standard source additionally identifies edit initialization's existing_comment_ids on relationship-selected comments before the later checked CommentFamily loader. Assigned discovery-0019 corroborates the same shared selector for styles, theme, numbering and fontTable under .bin names; its proof is limited to those four consumers, while earlier validated consumer paths remain retained. Assigned discovery-0027 additionally confirms relationship-selected settings bytes reaching settings_dom/settings_dom_xml and unchecked DOM construction on cache miss; settings is now a supplied validated consumer, whereas earlier recommendations remain historical source limitations. Assigned discovery-0028 supplies already-validated linked-textbox and diagram consumers: relationship-ID media targets at src/convert/mod.rs:17417-17428 and :17453-17464 are decoded and recursively parsed regardless of filename. The new source corroborates fontTable, theme, styles, numbering, settings, comments, notes and header/footer paths, and records that admission's content-type check covers the main part only. Assigned discovery-0031 additionally preserves strict normalization's extension-based pass-through: a relationship-selected fonts.bin remains unmodified before eager fontTable parsing. The raw unchecked parser's documented caller obligations are not themselves the finding.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled recursion through an admission bypass XML resource policy bypass\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674, CWE-20\n\nRemediation:\nApply active InputLimits at a centralized checked XML access/parse boundary for every semantic XML consumer regardless of filename, or resolve/classify and admit XML through actual content-type/relationship use. Cover theme, styles, numbering, converter comments/commentsExtended, notes and headers/footers; explicitly cover the now supplied validated settings_dom/settings_dom_xml cache-miss consumer, with earlier settings-only recommendations retained as historical source limitations. Preserve renamed-main checks, and enforce actual DOM construction depth or use iterative construction. Apply that same mandatory checked boundary to get_revisions and comparison notes parsing, including both footnotes and endnotes; propagate typed refusal under the active comparer InputLimits. Include pre_process_markup's relationship-selected notes at src/document_comparer.rs:4725-4750 and exposed Python get_revisions_json/WASM getRevisions; valid arbitrary part names remain supported. Include linked-textbox and diagram relationship targets in the mandatory filename-independent checked XML boundary before parse_xdocument and in regression coverage. These are now supplied validated affected consumers from discovery-0028; earlier sources' proposed-only status remains historical. Cover revision_processor RevisionIds collection and process_part for all six selected auxiliary buckets (headers, footers, endnotes, footnotes, comments and styles), including public revision acceptance/rejection. Explicitly include the now-confirmed fontTable loader (src/convert/font_table.rs:66-78; src/convert/mod.rs:806) in the mandatory checked XML boundary; parsing must be bounded before any font root/entry inspection. Explicitly cover comparison defined_style_ids (src/document_comparer.rs:4684-4696), relationship-selected footnotes/endnotes (4724-4750) and chart preprocessing (4861-4878), all reached through admitted nonidentical comparison inputs (6555-6569,6607-6625). Apply the same mandatory XML boundary before edit initialization's existing_comment_ids scan, not only in the later checked CommentFamily loader; preserve the effective checks at inspect::parse_part_within and edit::load_stories. Enforce the same checked boundary before settings DOM cache population, and preserve valid bounded nonstandard auxiliary filenames.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject an over-depth `.bin` theme with a typed XML refusal.\n- Cover styles, numbering, comments, footnotes and endnotes with nonstandard part extensions.\n- Cover relationship-named headers and footers using a non-XML extension.\n- A styles relationship to deeply nested styles.bin must return INVALID_XML under default limits.\n- Repeat for settings, theme, numbering, headers/footers, notes, and other relationship-selected XML consumers, including renamed main parts.\n- Use renamed styles/theme parts with depth 257 and 100000 and assert typed refusal before DOM construction.\n- Cover renamed comments, notes, headers and footers and preserve valid shallow arbitrary-name parts.\n- Run equivalent public Rust, Python and WASM rendering inputs with the active limit configuration.\n- Integration cases for nonstandard footnote/endnote extensions at and beyond a small explicit XML-depth limit.\n- Cover both get_revisions and compare with the same relationship-selected deep part.\n- Use footnotes/endnotes relationships to non-.xml names containing excessive depth or tag resources; assert typed refusal.\n- Retain valid nonstandard part names and ordinary depth-boundary behavior.\n- A styles relationship to deep styles.bin must refuse under max_xml_depth just like styles.xml.\n- Cover fontTable, settings, themes and story relationship consumers under renamed auxiliary parts and explicit raised limits.\n- Render a package with a styles relationship to deeply nested styles.bin and assert INVALID_XML before DOM construction.\n- Cover header/footer, notes, diagram and text-box relationship targets with nonstandard extensions and active depth/tag budgets.\n- Verify valid nonstandard auxiliary filenames continue to render.\n- Add deterministic regression inputs for the source-supported differential and assert a typed bounded refusal.\n- Verify ordinary compatible documents still process under unchanged limits.\n- An internal header/footer target named .bin with nesting above max_xml_depth must return INVALID_XML before DOM construction.\n- Repeat with custom part names and raised/lowered InputLimits; ordinary shallow parts must remain supported.\n- Repeat renamed-part admission regressions for styles, footnotes, endnotes and chart relationships in comparison preprocessing.\n- A deeply nested footnotes/endnotes part named notes.bin receives the same INVALID_XML refusal as notes.xml.\n- Custom-named auxiliary XML also honors attribute/tag budgets under active InputLimits.\n- Ordinary valid custom-named notes continue to compare.\n- Use relationship-routed auxiliary XML with a non-XML extension exceeding the configured depth; require INVALID_XML before DOM construction.\n- Rename styles,theme,numbering,fontTable XML to .bin and verify excess nesting/tag-policy inputs are refused before DOM construction.\n- Keep the renamed-main-part check and ordinary valid nonstandard auxiliary names supported.\n- Use non-.xml targets for each revision-bearing relationship and assert depth/tag violations are refused.\n- Cover custom main-part names, ordinary valid auxiliary targets, and preserved active limits.\n- Compare/render integration tests with renamed endnotes/footnotes/header/footer XML over configured depth must return typed INVALID_XML rather than enter recursive parsing.\n- Cover tag/attribute limits on renamed auxiliary parts and allowed renamed parts at exact depth boundary.\n- Deterministic boundary regression tests should assert typed refusal or bounded work for the identified tokenizer/classification/count discrepancy, with normal supported inputs preserved.\n- Render a DOCX with a deeply nested `numbering.bin` relationship target and assert an INVALID_XML refusal before DOM construction.\n- Retain support for nonstandard auxiliary filenames within the configured XML limits.\n- Apply the same renamed/deep-part refusal checks to fontTable, theme, styles and settings relationships.\n- Reject an over-depth font table targeted under a `.bin` name through an internal relationship.\n- Apply attribute/tag limits to renamed auxiliary XML parts.\n- Keep valid nonstandard auxiliary names supported while enforcing the same XML policy.\n- Exercise equivalent settings, styles, numbering and story consumers for filename-independent policy enforcement.\n- Accept/reject a document with a non-.xml auxiliary header, style or note exceeding max_xml_depth and assert typed refusal before DOM construction.\n- Repeat with attribute/tag policy violations and custom active limits.\n- Rename deeply nested headers/footnotes to .dat with valid internal relationships and assert typed XML-depth refusal for render and compare.\n- Verify custom-named valid auxiliary XML remains supported and active caller limits are preserved.\n- A fontTable relationship targeting deeply nested fonts.bin must fail with the same depth refusal as fonts.xml.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Centralize checked package XML access so consumers cannot silently bypass active policy.\n- Validate the representation actually consumed, using the consumer's type rather than filename suffix alone."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
