          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering a DOCX with a large table span can exhaust host memory\n\nA short `gridSpan`, `gridBefore`, or `gridAfter` value is parsed as an unrestricted column count. The renderer expands that numeric value into per-column vectors, so a small, shallow DOCX passing admission can request gigabytes of memory.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded input driven allocation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nValidate table spans and grid skips against a documented column/work budget before addition or allocation. Use checked arithmetic, bounded aggregate occupancy, and fallible allocation with a structured refusal.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject excessive gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter in public render paths.\n- Reject aggregate overflow and excessive combined spans.\n- Verify ordinary merged tables retain layout."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:63b13b0ddff48b772e15c0f0e23be0f99697773a6606591ef4306c42baa1ebe6"
