          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Document font names trigger quadratic persistent index rewrites\n\nMany distinct unknown font names in a DOCX cause the native renderer to record each miss and rewrite the entire growing font index separately. A document supplier can force quadratic CPU/disk work and grow persistent state across conversions without controlling host configuration.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic Complexity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nBatch font-index persistence once per conversion, bound/evict recorded unknown names and total index size, limit family-resolution work, and avoid rescanning/reformatting the entire index for each miss.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- With an in-memory fake index backend, verify many unique misses cause bounded writes per conversion and enforce family/index-size limits; retain intentional miss caching semantics."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:ce1b3749d3963583595ea8f49552d498b1974f6736410a71be0a7ae1d53728a3"
          },
          "properties": {
            "candidateId": "discovery-0022-font-index-growth",
            "category": "Algorithmic Complexity",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_5b24e6910eeca1b1d4367847",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_503e4bbee24bda6f06ef7cf1",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "algorithmic-complexity.font-index-rewrites",
          "ruleIndex": 4
        },
