          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering a small DOCX table can exhaust host memory\n\nAn untrusted DOCX author can set huge positive w:gridSpan, w:gridBefore or w:gridAfter counts in a small, shallow table. Rendering sums those counts into grid occupancy and directly sizes column, preference and merge vectors. Counts of 1000000000/1073741824 request about 4 GB/4 GiB for f32 columns; 4294967295 requests approximately 16 GiB before additional allocations, despite package admission. Assigned discovery-0031 corroborates the existing one-billion-column, 4,000,000,000-byte f32-vector framing through both span and row-skip inputs; these are static counts.\n Assigned discovery-0032 corroborates the live span and both synthetic row-skip paths, including merge-slot expansion; separate Markdown span clamping does not protect rendering.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions Unbounded allocation from document table metadata\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789, CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess. Propagate a caller-adjustable semantic column limit through all public rendering surfaces and charge later column/merge vectors to that same budget.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Enforce explicit maximum live cell spans, row skips, aggregate table columns and merge slots before any allocation. Use checked sums and a cumulative layout resource budget, returning a typed refusal when exceeded.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Check that a tiny table with an enormous gridSpan is refused before allocation.\n- Cover gridBefore/gridAfter, accumulated spans, and overflow boundaries.\n- Reject huge positive gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before allocation.\n- Reject checked aggregate row overflow and total table-grid budget overflow; valid small tables must preserve layout.\n- Excessive individual and cumulative spans/skips must refuse with bounded work.\n- Cover count overflow and 32-bit WASM.\n- Keep valid merged/skipped-column rendering.\n- Test excessive individual spans, row offsets and cumulative spans using tiny in-memory documents; assert typed refusal before allocation.\n- Test numeric overflow and valid boundary tables.\n- Integration-test huge cell spans and row skips through public rendering APIs and assert bounded typed refusal, including aggregate overflow.\n- Keep representative valid merged tables rendering correctly within the budget.\n- Tiny tables with very large gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter must fail with a resource-limit error before vector allocation.\n- Test cumulative spans exceeding the limit and arithmetic overflow; retain supported ordinary merged tables.\n- Reject huge gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter in otherwise small admitted DOCX files.\n- Cover aggregate span overflow and normal merged cells without large allocation.\n- Reject oversized gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter through public rendering APIs.\n- Verify cumulative occupancy and integer-overflow refusal on native and wasm32.\n- Preserve valid merged-cell and row-skip layouts.\n- Use a tiny admitted table with a very large positive gridSpan; assert a typed refusal before column or merge-state allocation.\n- Small table with huge gridSpan is refused before dense allocation.\n- Equivalent gridBefore and gridAfter inputs are refused.\n- Cumulative spans near overflow are refused using checked addition.\n- Normal merged tables remain supported at the documented inclusive limit.\n- Convert a minimal admitted DOCX with a huge gridSpan and assert a typed resource refusal before allocating.\n- Cover huge gridBefore/gridAfter and multiple individually valid spans whose sum exceeds the grid budget.\n- Refuse excessive cell spans and skipped-grid columns through each rendering binding.\n- Check cumulative spans and integer-overflow boundaries before allocation.\n- Reject huge gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter values before layout allocation.\n- Verify ordinary spans within the column budget still render, including stale-grid repair.\n- Reject huge gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter with a bounded typed refusal.\n- Cover multiple-cell sum overflow and combined column/merge allocation budgets.\n- Small admitted documents with oversized gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter must fail before allocating proportional buffers.\n- Verify cumulative spans exceeding the column/work budget are refused, including integer-overflow cases.\n- Render one-cell gridSpan and gridBefore/gridAfter probes with large positive values and assert a bounded refusal.\n- Test aggregate spans and arithmetic-overflow inputs; preserve valid small merged tables.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Bound derived dimensions and generated output independently from archive/XML input byte limits.\n- Use one semantic table-column policy for authored and synthesized cells.\n- Use shared semantic allocation budgets for document-controlled counts in every layout path."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:66b32ecf855841c34c763f7fa767b2677880df347e8efbd3bbce64582c6c2287"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans\nUnbounded allocation from document dimensions\nUnbounded allocation from document table metadata",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_9e40f23e742aa43493a0fb92",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_52c95ddfaa932739dde50b85",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.table-grid-span",
          "ruleIndex": 51
        },
