          "message": {
            "text": "Legacy DOC placeholder selection repeatedly rescans predictable document text\n\nDOC-to-DOCX conversion unconditionally searches all authored text for sequential predictable placeholder candidates, with no bounded selection algorithm. A few megabytes containing consecutive jubarteemptyparagraph0 through jubarteemptyparagraph99999 force about100000 increasingly long searches, occupying conversion CPU.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Quadratic internal placeholder selection\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nSkip placeholder selection when no empty paragraph requires it. Otherwise scan text once for occupied candidate suffixes or construct a delimiter using a bounded number of linear passes.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A document containing many sequential candidate tokens must perform bounded linear selection work, including documents with no empty paragraphs."
