          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Explicit Markdown revision IDs trigger quadratic run splitting\n\nA long unspaced insertion with proportionally many explicit revision IDs makes split_for_ids repeatedly search existing one-character tails, scan the remaining text, clone the long run and insert another tail. Work and copied bytes grow quadratically even though the Markdown input and resulting XML are linear in the number of IDs.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nCompute all split boundaries in one pass and build the final run vector once, moving/slicing source content rather than repeatedly cloning it. Apply an explicit revision-ID/work budget before conversion.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A large one-run/many-ID case uses bounded linear work while preserving exact IDs and text.\n- Boundary cases with more IDs than splittable text and Unicode characters preserve existing behavior."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:bfb4696e622d2a488bac94569024f9b8308b0ae5b2a5d8af4b4aff75f773cf07"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Algorithmic complexity",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_a10f0e5f40cc0a10cb3e3a1a",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_63f96fa56b40970da4ef6143",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "algorithmic-complexity.markdown-revision-split",
          "ruleIndex": 7
        },
