          "message": {
            "text": "Redaction succeeds while UTF-16 XML retains the removed text\n\nThe redact operation can return successful clean and redline documents while a supported BOM-marked UTF-16LE/BE auxiliary XML part still contains the same confidential text. Its XML leak branch uses lossy UTF-8 and misses the retained copy, which a recipient can recover after sharing. Even the scanner's no-root fallback searches the already lossily decoded string, so it cannot recover a multi-character value split by UTF-16 NUL bytes.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Incomplete removal of sensitive document information Incomplete sensitive data removal verification\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-212, CWE-201, CWE-200, CWE-176\n\nRemediation:\nDecode every XML part with the same BOM-aware policy as admission before semantic leak scanning. Fail closed on unsupported/undecodable/unparseable representations and retain raw UTF8 and both UTF16 byte-order checks as defense in depth. Use the same decoding across leak checks and package validation.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Redact visible body text while UTF16LE and UTF16BE customXml retains the same text; require REDACTION_LEAK.\n- Cover XML entities, split runs and encoding errors.\n- A document with no remaining copy must still redact successfully.\n- Redact a visible target while matching UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE custom XML remains; assert REDACTION_LEAK.\n- Verify the standalone leaks API reports encoded auxiliary copies and unsupported encodings fail closed.\n- Keep UTF-8 comments, processing instructions, entities and split-run matching; malformed/unsupported XML encodings must refuse rather than certify a partial scan.\n- Redact body text duplicated in UTF16LE and UTF16BE customXml XML and assert REDACTION_LEAK.\n- Assert successful outputs have no decoded copy across all supported XML encodings.\n- End-to-end redact refuses retained same-text UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE custom XML copies in both clean/redline.\n- Retain coverage for UTF-8 entities, split runs, attributes, comments and binary UTF-16.\n- Redact visible text while UTF16LE/BE custom XML copies remain; require REDACTION_LEAK.\n- Verify direct leaks reports both encoded XML variants.\n- Preserve ordinary split-run and decoded-entity detection.\n- Verify leaks finds multi-character text in BOM UTF16LE/BE .xml and .rels members.\n- Verify redact refuses when an untouched UTF16 XML part retains the removed value and succeeds only after every copy is removed.\n- Check that UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE XML text, attributes and comments are reported as leaks.\n- Assert a redaction plan refuses when a UTF-16 customXml part retains the redacted value.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Use the same accepted encoding rules at admission and security postcondition checks."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:90ee45d92b2d0b17b7bbc68ac050b82e5321412eafa7c5d754dcec617c868594"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Incomplete removal of sensitive document information\nIncomplete sensitive-data removal verification",
