          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Crafted MATH metrics can expand an equation into excessive glyphs\n\nA document with a crafted embedded math font can make inline fractions increase font size instead of reducing it. An enclosing stretchy delimiter then computes a huge extender count and stores one glyph per repetition, exhausting rendering resources despite shallow XML nesting. The assigned radical variant supplies finite arithmetic: unitsPerEm=1000, leaf yMax=1000, scriptPercentScaleDown=10000 (factor 100), ten nested inline numerator fractions at 12 pt, and one radical extender with fullAdvance=1 and zero overlap. The derived target/advance exceeds 1e23 and saturates to usize::MAX before the glyph loop. This is a supplied static construction, with no crafted-font acceptance or runtime demonstration.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled memory allocation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nValidate MATH scale percentages and metrics against supported finite ranges; reject extreme geometry and enforce a cumulative assembly-glyph budget before converting ratios to counts or allocating. Enforce hard per-assembly repetition caps as well as aggregate glyph bounds before floating-point-to-usize casts, and cover both unmarked radicals and delimiters with small positive extender advance above overlap.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Cover scale percentages above100 with nested inline fractions and delimiters.\n- Refuse assemblies exceeding a glyph budget before loops.\n- Retain normal valid MATH assembly behavior.\n- A finite embedded font with scriptScale>100% and nested fractions refuses within a bounded glyph budget.\n- Tiny positive extender advance plus large finite target cannot allocate beyond the configured assembly cap; normal radicals/delimiters remain supported.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Treat semantic font metrics and generated geometry as untrusted resource multipliers."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:c5259e8cc68c05677287d5127abd4cdb37c72cab4435354e4923d9e7443c1531"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled memory allocation",
            "confidence": "medium",
            "findingId": "csf_8c4451e023d8d194e7cae9a8",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_6a70f41e8474241d7a3f28f8",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "unbounded-expansion.math-glyph-assembly",
          "ruleIndex": 64
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
