              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Decoded relationship ampersands trigger quadratic target resolution\n\nA valid relationship Target containing N repeated &amp; values is decoded into N literal ampersands during metadata parsing. PartFs::resolve_rel_target decodes it again; unescape_xml_text searches the remaining suffix for a semicolon at every ampersand, causing about N(N-1)/2 probes before checking whether the target part exists.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nResolve stored relationship targets without a second XML decode. Independently replace the suffix-search entity helper with a single-pass implementation preserving unknown/incomplete references.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Valid escaped-ampersand targets are decoded exactly once.\n- Long strings of incomplete references are handled in linear work and retain the documented text."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:8a21fbb196b629c5a26d1240c231c405e06cd3a1ba69521fc5b3308ba93a7457"
          },
