          "message": {
            "text": "Repeated HTML chunk references bypass conversion memory budgets\n\nA DOCX can repeatedly reference one modest HTML part. The renderer admits the small original package, then copies and converts that chunk separately for every reference and concatenates all generated XML. The resulting allocation and work can exceed package budgets by orders of magnitude. For example, 10,000 short references to one 1 MiB ordinary HTML paragraph can imply roughly 10 GiB of generated XML; this is a static estimate, not a runtime measurement.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded post admission document expansion Unbounded logical document expansion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-409, CWE-770\n\nRemediation:\nMake altChunk expansion fallible under active cumulative expanded-byte, node/element, depth, work and occurrence budgets. Check contributions before conversion/allocation/append, including repeated internal relationships and MIME-decoded chunks, and validate generated XML under active limits before DOM construction. Caching may reduce repeated conversion CPU but cannot replace the total-output budget.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Use small explicit expansion limits to test repeated references to one ordinary HTML part at and above the budget.\n- Test distinct chunk parts and MIME-decoded chunks share the same cumulative budget.\n- Use multiple references to one modest internal HTML part and a small expansion budget; assert refusal before cumulative growth.\n- Verify normal repeated references and inclusive budget boundaries."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:3aa973cc9b4f20f384d21fd1d5a8b92312890f8ad3ac2bbd82d22e5367c5a0ae"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unbounded post-admission document expansion\nUnbounded logical document expansion",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_550f8cf900e415a773aa959d",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_6e78d485998c979efd988d4b",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
