                  "uri": "src/convert/altchunk.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 491,
                  "startLine": 489
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "HTML altChunk colspan causes unbounded generated XML expansion\n\nAn attacker-supplied DOCX can include a small HTML table whose colspan is an arbitrary usize. Conversion adds all spans and writes one gridCol element for each resulting column without an output or work budget. Large numeric spans cause excessive CPU and memory use after input admission has already succeeded.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unchecked input controlling resource consuming loops\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-606\n\nRemediation:\nBound colspan and the total table column count before iteration, use checked arithmetic, and enforce a cumulative generated-WML/output budget across each HTML chunk and document. Return a typed input-limit refusal before allocating oversized output.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Cover maximum allowed colspan, one above it, usize::MAX, and multiple spans whose sum overflows.\n- Test small admitted packages with oversized HTML spans and repeated chunks; assert bounded refusal under default limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:ab05a9485dd17a96d206924fce414938d132a51cd183a4939fb7bc0a5210914d"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unchecked input controlling resource-consuming loops",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_40b66860adb64bbff7afac76",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_7865799e5768135db96c1040",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "unbounded-altchunk-colspan-expansion",
          "ruleIndex": 60
        },
