          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Privacy scrubbing can return identifying data in valid relocated DOCX parts\n\nA document returned successfully by scrub can retain creator/editor identities, company/custom properties, revision authors, session IDs and people information when valid OPC relationships locate those parts outside conventional filenames or word/. Sharing the supposedly scrubbed output discloses the retained data. Supported relocated stories include content/main.xml and word/main.dat; a conventional prefix or .xml suffix is not semantic part identity.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Incomplete removal of sensitive information\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-212\n\nRemediation:\nDiscover all applicable metadata, people, comments, settings and story parts through relationships and content types. Apply the requested transforms to every discovered part and assert privacy-specific postconditions before returning success.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Relocate core/app/custom properties and main/story/people parts via valid relationships, then assert requested sensitive fields are absent.\n- Preserve safe refusal for active relocated-comment inconsistencies and test default and individual scrub selections.\n- Use a small deterministic document with extreme semantic values or alternate valid OPC paths and assert controlled refusal or complete selected sanitization before expensive processing."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:0d2fe9287150bb11a4ebc4960e779edc5ec456fa5a97615bc07d9129c9d91e73"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Incomplete removal of sensitive information",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_9885a1f1ab291001eef81daa",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_7f3d00607a53bf2eb6f54d23",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "incomplete-sanitization.relocated-opc-privacy-parts",
          "ruleIndex": 19
        },
