          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Intern-pool saturation duplicates long namespace URIs per element\n\nA shallow valid XML input can first fill the 16,384-entry intern pool with distinct short names, then introduce a new 8,192-byte namespace URI and repeat tiny elements in that namespace. Once the pool is full, each element retains a fresh URI allocation. About 131,072 elements retain at least 1 GiB of URI bytes from less than 1 MiB of source.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Namespace memory amplification\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-770\n\nRemediation:\nShare active namespace URI allocations directly from parser scope independently of global-pool capacity, or use bounded per-document interning with explicit refusal when storage budget is exhausted.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A bounded regression for the identified input returns a normal refusal or bounded result before large allocation/recursion.\n- Ordinary documents at the active boundary continue to parse under caller-selected limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:798889e12bf3ed5d95059dae7447e985e2d13b81ef117e1832447ffd59177fa0"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Namespace memory amplification",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_b6323ea4d1b9deec7fd1691b",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_80e6df8d8e9ec9329f8d5908",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.xml-namespace-interning",
          "ruleIndex": 52
        },
        {
