                  "startLine": 531
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering nonstandard auxiliary XML parts bypasses admission depth limits\n\nAn attacker-supplied DOCX can name an auxiliary styles part with a non-XML extension. Admission skips XML checks for that part, but rendering follows its styles relationship and passes the bytes to an unchecked recursive DOM parser. Deep nesting can exhaust the host stack despite normal admission.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: XML resource policy bypass\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nValidate every selected XML part immediately before DOM construction with active InputLimits, or classify all XML parts using content types and relationships in admission. Apply the same policy to auxiliary styles, themes, numbering and other XML consumers regardless of filename.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A non-XML-suffixed deep styles target must return the same policy refusal as styles.xml.\n- Test all auxiliary relationship-selected XML consumers with nonstandard filenames and malformed/over-budget XML.\n- Retain valid nonstandard names without silently skipping content."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:2f9e632a5108a7c880fcf8c90a839ce4fbfc02d97ca968d588809cc149937d42"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "XML resource policy bypass",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_c1fe8475183ebde207aa0c59",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_81cf4f672ad07251b07c2a48",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "xml-policy-bypass.auxiliary-part-extension",
          "ruleIndex": 83
