          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "WMF record-boundary failures amplify polygon work and retained text\n\nRendering a DOCX with a crafted placeable WMF lets short declared records consume payload from later records, which the outer parser then revisits. Polygon/polypolygon/polyline records can cause billions of coordinate decodes from roughly 512 KiB; EXTTEXTOUT/TEXTOUT records can retain hundreds of megabytes of overlapping owned strings from roughly 205.6 KB. The common missing record-local boundary bypasses the canvas cap and original package budgets. A further framing uses alternating six-byte EXTTEXTOUT and unknown 0xFFFF record headers to claim 65,535 text bytes from subsequent records, implying several GiB of retained strings from roughly 1 MiB of media; this is a static estimate. A supplied 7-word EXTTEXTOUT framing uses 65536 fourteen-byte records plus a 65535-byte suffix in less than 1 MiB and requests about 4 GiB of decoded characters; nonzero mapping dimensions and nonblank text are required. This is a static estimate. Assigned discovery-0031 supplies an additional static eight-byte TEXTOUT framing with a 65535-byte claimed string and overlapping following bytes. About 1 MiB can request multiple gigabytes of retained text; valid whole-file reads, nonblank text and nonzero mapping extents remain required. No out-of-bounds memory read is asserted.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption Malformed record length permits overlapping allocation amplification Missing record local length validation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-1284, CWE-770, CWE-20, CWE-130\n\nRemediation:\nConfine every WMF handler, including field, font, string and geometry reads, to a slice limited to its checked declared record extent. Before allocation validate fixed fields, ring/point counts and coordinate arrays, EXTTEXTOUT options/optional rectangle and text count, and TEXTOUT padded string plus trailing coordinates against that slice using checked arithmetic. Refuse inconsistent records before decoding/rasterization/replay and enforce cumulative decoded-text, record and total geometry/work budgets. Keep the already bounded EMF behavior.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Short WMF polygon, polypolygon and polyline records claiming following-record points must refuse before processing points.\n- Repeated malformed records must consume work proportional to declared bytes, with EMF behavior retained.\n- Deterministic parser tests with short declared records and text counts extending into the next record must refuse safely.\n- Cover EXTTEXTOUT options/rectangle, TEXTOUT padding and record-local geometry counts with small resource budgets.\n- Reject EXTTEXTOUT and TEXTOUT strings extending into the next record.\n- Reject cross-record polygon/polypolygon/polyline coordinates and validate large valid records within aggregate text/geometry budgets.\n- Use existing in-memory WMF fixtures to ensure six-byte EXTTEXTOUT/TEXTOUT cannot read subsequent records.\n- Verify repeated undersized records produce no retained text.\n- Retain valid text rendering tests and exercise cumulative text-budget refusal.\n- Small malformed EXTTEXTOUT and TEXTOUT records must be rejected without reading following bytes.\n- Repeated short records must remain within deterministic cumulative allocation/work limits.\n- Verify valid WMF text still renders through public PDF/PNG APIs.\n- Exercise short TEXTOUT, EXTTEXTOUT, POLYGON, POLYPOLYGON and POLYLINE records with sufficient trailing bytes; require refusal without consuming the next record.\n- Refuse textout/exttextout/polygon/polypolygon/polyline counts extending beyond their record despite sufficient following file bytes.\n- Verify repeated small records cannot amplify trailing content into unbounded retained output.\n- Refuse EXTTEXTOUT and TEXTOUT whose counts or coordinate fields extend past their own record even when still inside the file.\n- Ensure many valid records hit a bounded aggregate text budget and ordinary WMF text stays supported.\n- Reject header-only TEXTOUT/EXTTEXTOUT records even when later file bytes can satisfy their reads.\n- Bound aggregate extracted text and test valid records exactly at declared boundaries.\n- Exercise undersized text records using small harmless limits and assert refusal without reading following-record bytes.\n- Verify aggregate text budgets and normal EXTTEXTOUT/TEXTOUT records; avoid allocating attacker-sized outputs.\n- Undersized TEXTOUT/EXTTEXTOUT refuses before text retention.\n- POLYGON/POLYPOLYGON/POLYLINE counts cannot consume following records.\n- Valid WMF and EMF rendering remains supported.\n- Reject text counts extending beyond EXTTEXTOUT/TEXTOUT record end even when bytes remain in the file.\n- Reject polygon, polypolygon and polyline counts extending beyond their records.\n- Verify repeated short records cannot copy overlapping trailing bytes into retained text.\n- Keep valid WMF rendering and existing extreme-coordinate/record-size tests.\n- Assert EXTTEXTOUT/TEXTOUT counts beyond record end are refused even if the file has sufficient trailing bytes.\n- Exercise polygon/polypolygon/polyline/font records with truncated declared payloads.\n- Assert repeated small records cannot create decoded-text output disproportionate to valid payload bytes.\n- Short TEXTOUT/EXTTEXTOUT and geometry records whose counts extend into the next record must be rejected before copying or iteration.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Bound the actual representation depth and processing work at the consuming boundary.\n- Pass bounded record slices to all metafile handlers instead of exposing the entire backing file."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:4e33ec35b897858d913d90a89cc2aee186a44ffeb2ddc655345086268a4a919e"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled resource consumption\nMalformed record length permits overlapping allocation amplification\nMissing record-local length validation",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_80edacafa6b67d4864116a38",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_81fd3bd15146f646c7d5a8db",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-amplification.wmf-record-payload",
          "ruleIndex": 40
        },
