                  "startLine": 235
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Python CLI output writes follow substituted symlinks\n\nPython CLI output checks Path.exists separately from Path.write_bytes. A lower-trust actor controlling the output directory can substitute a symlink after the check, causing victim-authority truncation of another file; a dangling link can also redirect creation without --force.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Check then write symlink race\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-367\n\nRemediation:\nUse exclusive no-clobber creation for absent outputs and private staging with atomic rename when replacement is authorized. Hold the destination parent and avoid reopening a checked final path with symlink-following truncation.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A pre-placed staging/output symlink never changes its referent.\n- A destination created after a no-force check is refused atomically; authorized replacement installs at the selected entry.\n- Verify final-path and parent-substitution behavior on supported platforms."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:fe347a16fff26b690fd9b69364c2a664da1fa505edd8101afdcba6b84e2f92d6"
          },
          "properties": {
