          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Public Strict-format probe inflates unbounded document headers\n\nThe public main_part_is_strict helper reads word/document.xml without admission or an inflation/preamble cap. A compressible oversized/unfinished root opening tag or long XML comment keeps the last '<' at offset zero; the full growing head remains retained and is repeatedly scanned until the root tag completes or EOF, allowing memory/CPU exhaustion for direct library consumers. The assigned audit establishes direct public-library exposure and found no in-repository production caller; ordinary rendering is not claimed to call this detector.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded decompression\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-409, CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nApply bounded admission before indexing/inflation and explicit cumulative inflated-byte/preamble/work limits to this public helper. Use a streaming lexical probe with bounded retained state for comments, declarations and chunk-spanning root tags; refuse excessive probes with a checked/limited API and safe default limits.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Test oversized compressed opening tags under a small budget and retain valid within-budget preambles.\n- Long compressed comments must hit a deterministic input/work bound.\n- A chunk-spanning legal prolog should be recognized with constant retained state.\n- An unfinished oversized opening tag terminates classification within a bounded budget.\n- Long legitimate preambles retain supported behavior without unbounded head growth.\n- Feed an over-budget compressed opening tag and assert a bounded refusal/false result before large retention.\n- Test long preambles and quote-aware delimiter parsing with explicit limits.\n- Use a small deterministic document with extreme semantic values or alternate valid OPC paths and assert controlled refusal or complete selected sanitization before expensive processing.\n- Refuse an oversized root start tag under a small configurable input policy without inflating it fully.\n- Verify long bounded preambles and ordinary Strict/Transitional roots remain classified correctly.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Require every public compressed-input probe to share admission and incremental work budgets."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:5dead229e7ab373cadb63ef62a70834170096c36d9f4c9e9b2da781019f05349"
