          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded numbering levels drive billions of renderer operations\n\nAn admitted DOCX paragraph requesting ilvl=4294967295 with an ordinary level-0 numbering definition makes resolve_ilvl perform about 4.3 billion lookups. Declaring that huge level instead causes next_marker to populate counters for every preceding level, exhausting memory.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Excessive iteration from numbering metadata\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-834\n\nRemediation:\nValidate paragraph, style, abstract-level and override ilvl values against supported numbering levels before use. Find a parent by examining declared keys and avoid populating nonexistent levels. Return a normal refusal for unsupported values.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Render rejects u32::MAX paragraph and declared numbering levels before iteration.\n- Undefined ordinary levels still resolve to supported parents; Markdown remains bounded."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:19f3d3ce5d86602493d051425f21894062545e0ba5fe6cf869a926fed8fcac0e"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Excessive iteration from numbering metadata",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_64287538a7a91a3131e41cf3",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_8846225e88d395ac76fc0d98",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.numbering-level",
          "ruleIndex": 49
        },
        {
