          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Python plan recording follows predictable temporary-file symlinks\n\nPlan recording writes to .<resolved-plan-name>.<pid>.partial without exclusive creation. A lower-trust writer of the plan directory can pre-place that name as a link to a victim-writable file; partial.write_bytes truncates the referent before os.replace executes.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Insecure temporary file creation symlink following\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-61\n\nRemediation:\nCreate unpredictable private staging or exclusive temporary files through a held parent handle; retain the created handle, verify bytes and atomically rename that file into place. Never open a preexisting staging pathname for truncation.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A pre-placed staging/output symlink never changes its referent.\n- A destination created after a no-force check is refused atomically; authorized replacement installs at the selected entry.\n- Verify final-path and parent-substitution behavior on supported platforms."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:9114a44ac59a72fab97d8de52f9ca81a932cd745a8e3db5206ea2b7d1f18a219"
