          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Converting a small HTML altChunk can exhaust memory\n\nAn attacker-controlled HTML table colspan inside a DOCX altChunk is parsed as an unrestricted usize and expanded into one generated WML gridCol per column. A short decimal span can force billions of XML tags before rendering, bypassing admission limits on the original package.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Resource exhaustion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nReject excessive per-cell and aggregate HTML column spans using checked arithmetic before output generation, and charge all altChunk-generated XML against an explicit expansion budget.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Integration-test a tiny internal HTML chunk with a span above the configured cap and require a typed refusal before expansion.\n- Test exact span/output-budget limits, multiple-cell sum overflow and ordinary colspan rendering."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:88e44e7c347bf0dd4a099c6f47578ed13d0eb8fd55ad745c5e3ad6bed66c28bb"
          },
