          "message": {
            "text": "Python and npm plan recording follows precreated staging symlinks\n\nBoth command adapters write plan JSON through a predictable .<plan-name>.<pid>.partial pathname without exclusive creation or link refusal. A local directory writer can preplace a symlink and cause an unrelated file writable by the CLI process to be truncated before the final rename.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Insecure temporary file creation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-377\n\nRemediation:\nUse exclusive unpredictable private staging and hold directory/file handles until atomic publication. Reuse native publication for Python and implement equivalent exclusive/no-follow staging for Node; never reopen an attacker-controlled temporary pathname.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Integration-test a precreated staging symlink and assert an unrelated sentinel stays unchanged.\n- Verify valid and refused recordings, dry-run, cleanup and atomic replacement with a deterministic fake publication backend in unit tests."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:11adbd284f181db80f68c0d5a0fe857520bebbdf080035dab2ae01ea547bc82d"
          },
