          "message": {
            "text": "Windows Markdown image checks can contact an external share before rejecting it\n\nDocument-controlled image paths are canonicalized before resource-root containment is checked. On Windows, a decoded UNC path replaces the trusted root and canonicalization opens the remote path, causing outbound filesystem contact even when the image is later refused.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unintended remote filesystem access before resource authorization\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-918\n\nRemediation:\nReject decoded absolute, prefixed, UNC and root-relative destinations before any ambient filesystem operation, and resolve accepted relative resources through the held directory capability. Apply the same policy to diagnostic-only paths.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Verify encoded UNC, verbatim UNC and root-relative destinations are rejected before any filesystem resolver is called on Windows.\n- Cover convert, compare, patch and text-diff diagnostics and preserve allowed in-root relative images."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:63d217ec85d1160b7811df7dc98a7a98a322f24835fbe8eefe5e0c27ce244b01"
          },
          "properties": {
