          "message": {
            "text": "Tracked-edit audit parses permission-bearing XML before admission\n\naudit_tracked opens both packages and checks dropped permission ranges before reject_changes later admits edited bytes. When a legitimate original contains permStart/permEnd, the corresponding edited XML reaches raw recursive parsing first, enabling a deeply nested edited part to exhaust the host stack.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nAdmit both original and edited packages before check_dropped_permissions, or replace its raw parse_part with checked parsing under active limits.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A bounded regression for the identified input returns a normal refusal or bounded result before large allocation/recursion.\n- Ordinary documents at the active boundary continue to parse under caller-selected limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:edc90ad05682bec226632bd31e62d1f922d669409f64d5ea4404372fc963f54e"
