          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Nested Markdown header or footer fields can overflow the conversion stack\n\nAn attacker-controlled header/footer scalar can contain thousands of nested short field results. The Markdown story writer recursively materializes each result without a nesting limit, causing stack exhaustion or substantial repeated scanning before DOCX output validation.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled recursion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nEnforce a field-result nesting and generated-XML budget before materialization, returning a typed conversion refusal. Prefer an explicit stack and avoid rescanning nested suffixes at every level.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject excessive nested fields inside one header/footer scalar without overflowing the stack.\n- Retain normal nested field results, escaped markers and the existing map/instruction limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:a9982b0fc2388bd518df08679af0c0e23ac389338d2ac026bb2d9e0cf12f2f41"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled recursion",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_5ca5660e582c260e59b28647",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_a133211ccbce0ff28b9c3d44",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "uncontrolled-recursion.markdown-story-fields",
          "ruleIndex": 73
        },
