          "message": {
            "text": "npm plan recording follows a predictable staging symlink\n\nWhen recording plan operations, the npm CLI writes to a basename/PID staging path without exclusive creation. A local attacker who can create entries in that directory can redirect the write to an unrelated file writable by the CLI user.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Symlink following in temporary file publication\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-59, CWE-377, CWE-61\n\nRemediation:\nCreate an unpredictable private staging directory next to the plan and open the staged regular file exclusively. Write through its held descriptor and rename only that file. At minimum refuse every preexisting staging entry using exclusive creation rather than default truncating writes.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Preexisting partial symlink must cause refusal without changing its referent.\n- Concurrent staging-name collisions must fail safely.\n- Valid plan recording and dry-run behavior remain correct.\n- Integration-test a preplanted link at the legacy PID partial name; an unrelated file must remain unchanged.\n- Ensure staging files are exclusively created in a private random directory.\n- Retain documented final plan symlink resolution while refusing existing staging links.\n- Use a small deterministic document with extreme semantic values or alternate valid OPC paths and assert controlled refusal or complete selected sanitization before expensive processing."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:73d5631ef01f4e0f8a36ca3404776bcde8db4c2a872f4f4581d319002a2cee42"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Symlink following in temporary-file publication",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_58625a5255dafe3f4e5744ea",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_a5fe9b5097f48bb1da8d70f6",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "symlink-following.plan-staging",
          "ruleIndex": 54
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
