          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering a long paragraph performs quadratic suffix scans\n\nWrapping computes every remaining token suffix before line breaking, even when the paragraph contains no tabs and does not need suffix widths.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nCompute suffix widths in a single reverse pass with resets at tab boundaries, or skip suffix work for tab-free segments.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A large no-tab paragraph performs a linear number of suffix-width operations.\n- Center/right tab alignment retains correct suffix widths across consecutive tabs and explicit breaks."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:7b5b800d48c3e7de5837d026d836a6795c2a9b09a524f12b1de20520ed33b250"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled resource consumption",
            "confidence": "high",
