                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared font-index parent permits symlink-directed cache staging writes\n\nWhen an operator configures the font index in a directory writable by a lower-trust local actor, FontIndex::save writes to the predictable font-index.tsv.<pid>.tmp path with fs::write. A planted symlink redirects a victim-authority write before rename. Default per-user cache directories do not by themselves establish this prerequisite.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Insecure temporary file creation symlink following\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-61\n\nRemediation:\nCreate unpredictable private staging or exclusive temporary files through a held parent handle; retain the created handle, verify bytes and atomically rename that file into place. Never open a preexisting staging pathname for truncation.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A pre-placed staging/output symlink never changes its referent.\n- A destination created after a no-force check is refused atomically; authorized replacement installs at the selected entry.\n- Verify final-path and parent-substitution behavior on supported platforms."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:d1d7f7c22a764d26c5aa4b4f5dd9c341e78cf769a152fa8ea4dcabf7746c3625"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Insecure temporary-file creation / symlink following",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_d633eef7259aae77e07e54f3",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_a88decd92294bf825cf5582e",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "filesystem.font-index-predictable-staging",
          "ruleIndex": 17
        },
