          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Reference metadata stamping builds oversized ZIP indexes before refusal\n\nPass a reference DOCX/ZIP with far more than 10000 entries to `docx_stamp` or `markdown_stamp`. The helper constructs the ZIP index and allocates,traverses and sorts archive-wide extent metadata before checking the entry cap,so an otherwise rejected reference can consume substantial CPU and memory first.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Resource limits applied after expensive ZIP parsing\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nApply a documented compressed-input and declared-entry preindex budget before opening metadata ZIPs,or enforce it centrally in Package::open. Preserve best-effort absent-metadata behavior only after a cheap bounded refusal.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reference archives exceeding the entry cap are refused before ZIP index/extent construction.\n- Oversized compressed reference input fails cheaply; ordinary metadata/front-matter precedence remains unchanged.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Place resource admission before allocations that scale with attacker-controlled archive metadata."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:e4f18d46f474d582e00ce762494b3d22817d32d1482b7d1683ce7a6cf2ee4474"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Resource limits applied after expensive ZIP parsing",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_08670176ab69a0d459ba1059",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_afd733cb7aa96aefebb8a3cf",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "zip-preindex-budget-bypass",
          "ruleIndex": 87
        },
