          "message": {
            "text": "Large page coordinates make border rendering loop without progress\n\nFinite page dimensions and margins from DOCX can place a dotted border at coordinates where its f32 increment rounds to zero. Rendering then loops indefinitely while appending drawing operations, exhausting memory.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Nonprogressing floating point rendering loop\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-835\n\nRemediation:\nValidate finite, reasonable page/margin/border geometry before layout. Use a bounded integer segment count instead of open-ended float accumulation, enforce a maximum border-operation budget, and explicitly refuse any step that cannot advance.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Large finite coordinates with dotted/dashed borders must refuse promptly.\n- Cover nonfinite values and huge segment counts separately.\n- Keep ordinary supported page-border styles rendering correctly."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:f65cebb69c4ab826cfa21adfeee6c35b894d234e6727eabd89c7cbb46a73bf8f"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Nonprogressing floating-point rendering loop",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_a9b4e9d87eb567391149dad1",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_b4c52aa382593e76ce3893e2",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "infinite-loop.page-border-float",
          "ruleIndex": 20
        },
