          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "HTML altChunk colspan expands into unbounded generated XML\n\nA DOCX HTML altChunk containing a one-cell colspan=2147483647 table causes the renderer to generate billions of gridCol elements after package admission. Generated WML has no byte or column budget, causing extreme CPU and memory use before DOM construction.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded allocation from table dimensions\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nBound HTML table column counts with checked sums and cap generated altChunk WML bytes during emission. Propagate a typed refusal to the renderer before expansion or parsing.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A small HTML/MHT table with excessive colspan refuses before generating a large WML string.\n- Column-budget and generated-byte-budget exact boundaries retain valid ordinary tables."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:40c14d15e118c5213584a21b653d422e22c20c9b5b1323fac865f7e685f028aa"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unbounded allocation from table dimensions",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_656f2c09e37719ab674c7d01",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_b8c00e467eaf0bd1ef9b7046",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.table-grid-span",
          "ruleIndex": 51
        },
