          "message": {
            "text": "Converting legacy DOC text with a long numeric prefix causes quadratic work\n\nFor each period or closing parenthesis, the Markdown escaper rescans the full preceding text. A long digit prefix followed by many periods repeatedly scans the same digits, consuming disproportionate CPU on a small legacy DOC.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nTrack a running all-ASCII-digits prefix flag while iterating once, or identify the sole initial numeric-list delimiter once. Preserve escaping behavior with linear work.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Use a deterministic examined-character counter for long digits-plus-periods and digits-plus-parentheses inputs.\n- Assert ordinary numeric-list escaping remains identical.\n- Use a small deterministic document with extreme semantic values or alternate valid OPC paths and assert controlled refusal or complete selected sanitization before expensive processing."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:2e4d77139888d5f78c7179edf0f3c04d8a1114c10e9fcaa2a114f6671e0f8aab"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Algorithmic complexity denial of service",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_85e0853b68d29e45897292e3",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_b9b90b71699f16ab313cb741",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "legacy-doc-markdown-prefix-complexity",
          "ruleIndex": 24
        },
