          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Scrubbing can silently preserve identifying UTF-16 core and app properties\n\nAccepted UTF-16 core/app property XML is loaded through a lossy UTF-8 helper. The DOM has no root, so the scrubber silently skips the selected part and can return success with creator/editor or company/manager data still present.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Incomplete metadata removal after XML decoding failure\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-201\n\nRemediation:\nUse a shared encoding-aware XML decoder for selected metadata parts, and fail closed when a selected part cannot be parsed or requested identifying values remain. Handle both UTF-16 endiannesses consistently with admission.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Scrub BOM-marked UTF-16LE/BE conventional core/app properties and assert requested identifying fields are removed.\n- Assert selected metadata parse failure produces a controlled refusal rather than a successful unchanged part."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:af8fcf503db849820c95a3d2431f7265ecbd8c97a5a639c67ef275db54b2adbb"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Incomplete metadata removal after XML decoding failure",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_3b8aeff5efd1bfbd5ccfd3dd",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_bada53ff4997b2ec589a32a3",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "metadata-scrubbing.utf16-xml",
          "ruleIndex": 28
        },
