          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Legacy edit-anchor searches compare long prefixes at every character\n\nLegacy plan resolution searches for an anchor with starts_with at every character position, including its normalized fallback. A repetitive paragraph paired with a long near-matching anchor can force quadratic CPU work before the plan is refused or applied.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nUse a linear-time substring matcher for exact and normalized legacy anchors, reusing the v2 KMP approach, while preserving overlapping-hit semantics and source-offset mapping. Add explicit cumulative matching-work limits where needed.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Use deterministic comparison counts for long common-prefix nonmatches on both exact and normalized legacy paths.\n- Preserve overlapping hits, Unicode offsets and occurrence selection."
          },
