          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering a small DOCX table can allocate billions of columns\n\nThe renderer accepts w:gridSpan and row grid skip values as unbounded usize counts. table_block sizes its column vectors from the summed spans, so a small admitted DOCX can request multi-gigabyte allocations or a capacity-overflow abort in PDF/PNG/report conversion.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Resource exhaustion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nValidate gridSpan and row gridBefore/gridAfter counts against a bounded aggregate table-column budget before any arithmetic, iteration or allocation. Use checked addition and fallible allocations with typed conversion errors.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Integration-test a minimal admitted WML table with an excessive gridSpan and require bounded refusal.\n- Cover excessive gridBefore/gridAfter, overflowing row sums, merge bookkeeping and exact accepted limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:ea89f4ad1c2e4cba678434d825bd6c3a736308ae6f4a75d78850407ec6843eed"
