            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:altchunk-consumer"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/convert/mod.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 798,
                  "startLine": 789
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded HTML colspan exhausts memory during DOCX rendering\n\nAn untrusted DOCX can reference a tiny HTML altChunk with a billion-column colspan. The converter accepts the integer without an upper bound and emits one grid-column XML element per declared column before parsing the expanded body, exhausting memory and CPU despite package admission.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nReject or cap colspan before storing it, use checked totals, and enforce a total generated grid/output budget before expanding HTML/MHT chunks. Return a typed conversion refusal for oversized tables.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A tiny altChunk with colspan 1000000000 must fail before large output allocation.\n- Cover inclusive limits, cumulative spans across cells, integer overflow, nested tables, and both HTML and MHT import."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:d92782bb3232c83f4fe995b2c5939869548724e86da5e34eecf7eaeabd0a71d8"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled resource consumption",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_8dc0178c218380a4337cf074",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_d156d672f1eb2d924ce50b0c",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.altchunk-colspan",
          "ruleIndex": 41
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
