            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Non-XML auxiliary filenames bypass admission before recursive parsing\n\naccept_revisions and reject_revisions admit a DOCX, but the admission XML scan covers .xml/.rels names plus only the main part's alternate extension. A header/footer/notes/comments/styles relationship can point to header.dat containing deep XML; revision processing parses it without depth validation, permitting native stack exhaustion or a WASM trap.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nValidate every actual XML part under active InputLimits immediately before DOM construction, or use content types/relationships to include all consumed XML in admission. Cover headers, footers, notes, comments and styles regardless filename.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Accept/reject refuse over-depth .dat auxiliary parts with the normal XML-depth error.\n- The same refusal applies to excessive auxiliary tag/namespace fields while valid alternate filenames continue to work."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:9c205e11eb20fea1a99aef538e0bb1ca87661d4429a92950c21ca2be56e64618"
          },
