          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "HTML selector groups multiply CSS values into excessive memory\n\nA DOCX HTML altChunk can combine one large CSS property value with thousands of grouped selectors. The importer deep-copies the complete property map into each selector, consuming gigabytes even if none of the rules are used. A supplied framing uses 4096 distinct selectors and one 1 MiB value for about 4 GiB of retained value storage, excluding overhead; this is a static estimate. Additional supplied static framing: 10000 distinct short selectors sharing a 1 MiB property imply about 10 GiB of retained values from approximately 1.1 MiB HTML; this is not a memory measurement.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled memory allocation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789, CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nShare immutable declaration maps/values across grouped selectors and enforce cumulative selector, rule and declaration-byte budgets before allocation. Enforce value-length limits and discard unsupported properties before retaining them; unused selectors and properties must still count toward the aggregate budget.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Parse large grouped selectors and verify declaration buffers are shared or a typed budget refusal occurs.\n- Cover unused and unsupported CSS properties as well as normal cascading.\n- Reject or boundedly process thousands of distinct selectors sharing a large declaration value.\n- Ensure unused CSS rules are subject to the same storage budget and ordinary comma-separated selectors still render correctly.\n- Assert that many selectors sharing a large declaration block remain bounded or are refused before multiplication.\n- Cover unused selectors, unsupported property names, multiple style blocks, and valid boundary inputs.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Account for multiplicative representation expansion at parser boundaries."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:c75a04b6bd2121edf755a4d080a33061276f3bbbf18e3aa478e3cde4fe0b388a"
          },
