          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded document table spans exhaust memory during rendering\n\nUntrusted direct OOXML gridSpan/gridBefore/gridAfter and imported HTML/MHT colspan values become unrestricted output column counts. Tiny metadata can request a billion columns, driving dense column/preference/merge vectors or pre-DOM gridCol XML generation before derived-output budgets. These independently reachable paths require controls before both import generation and layout; package byte/depth admission does not bound their semantic expansion.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nEnforce practical per-cell span/row-skip and checked cumulative table/grid/output budgets across direct OOXML gridSpan/gridBefore/gridAfter and HTML/MHT colspan. Apply the common limit before HTML generation and before RawCell, column/preference/merge allocation or span-sized work; use checked sums and col+span arithmetic and return a typed conversion refusal. Neither importer-only nor later layout-only checking is sufficient. Use fallible allocation/reservation within those bounds so capacity failures become typed refusals. Carry the caller-configurable column/occupancy budget through every table source and enforce a generated-XML/output ceiling before altChunk materialization.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A tiny altChunk with colspan 1000000000 must fail before large output allocation.\n- Cover inclusive limits, cumulative spans across cells, integer overflow, nested tables, and both HTML and MHT import.\n- Cover direct OOXML gridSpan with tiny/no initial tblGrid, gridBefore/gridAfter variants, and merge bookkeeping as well as imported colspan.\n- Test default public PDF and PNG/render entry points with small DOCX tables containing excessive gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter values; require typed refusal before allocation.\n- Test cumulative multi-cell spans and machine-width boundary values, plus legitimate merged tables within the budget.\n- Test boundary and over-limit gridSpan/gridBefore/gridAfter via public rendering APIs; assert bounded refusal without allocating attacker-sized storage.\n- Test combined row spans and arithmetic overflow; preserve ordinary merged-cell rendering.\n- Use small deterministic HTML fixtures to verify a large numeric colspan is rejected before output construction; test exact column-budget boundaries, overflow of aggregate spans, and normal merged-cell behavior.\n- Test native gridSpan, gridBefore/gridAfter and combined-row occupancy at and beyond the budget, as well as aggregate arithmetic overflow.\n- Use a small deterministic document with extreme semantic values or alternate valid OPC paths and assert controlled refusal or complete selected sanitization before expensive processing."
          },
