          "message": {
            "text": "Mixed edit plans repeat redacted text in another operation's report\n\nA successful plan that redacts sensitive text and edits nearby words can remove the text from both DOCX files while retaining it in the adjacent edit's source-context field. The generated report and report-bearing MCP response disclose that text despite the documented privacy guarantee.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Sensitive information exposure\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-200\n\nRemediation:\nApply redaction-aware sanitization to every report, refusal and diagnostic field after resolving the full plan, including other operations' contexts. Check the final serialized reports for all redaction needles before publication, omitting unsafe context when needed.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Extend the existing adjacent redact+replace test to inspect EditReport, JSONL, CLI report.jsonl and MCP report.json/response for the removed identifier.\n- Check mixed-plan failure outcomes and diagnostics as well as successful reports.\n- Extend tests/scrub_and_redact.rs:353 mixed redact/replace case to assert secret absence from report JSON, JSONL and failure outcomes.\n- Extend the existing mixed redact/replace fixture to assert serialized reports omit the removed value.\n- Cover sibling-operation refusals and MCP/native/Python/WASM report serialization."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:a6e0691cb48343cf0a84b89820c32446b4424798e4ac81a02f9aba17eea4cc38"
          },
