          "message": {
            "text": "Repeated compressed-image references can exhaust renderer memory\n\nA DOCX can reference one highly compressible embedded image many times. Conversion independently decodes and retains an owned pixel buffer per reference, then clones buffers into page operations. Package byte limits and per-page pixel limits do not bound this aggregate decoded memory. The assigned source confirms image 0.25.10's default 512 MiB allocation limit applies separately to each decode. A 4096x4096 RGBA raster requires about 64 MiB per occurrence and a hundred references retain gigabytes; authored drawing/page extents do not cap intrinsic decoded storage. These are supplied static counts. Assigned discovery-0031 supplies a static 1000-reference framing for one ordinary solid 2048x2048 PNG: about 11.7 GiB of retained RGB alone before page painting. Group-picture, VML-preview and picture-bullet paths also independently decode resources; destination MAX_PAGE_PIXELS and per-decode limits do not bound aggregate retention.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Missing aggregate decoded media resource budget\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-770, CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nApply a conversion-wide decoded-pixel/byte budget before decoding or retaining media, cache decoded parts by source and transformation, and use shared immutable samples in layout/display operations. Count transformed and temporary buffers against the same budget. Apply the same sharing and aggregate accounting to group-picture, VML-preview and picture-bullet consumers, keyed by effective transformation; retain all earlier display-list/temporary-buffer accounting.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Assert repeated references share decoded sample storage and remain under an aggregate budget.\n- Refuse a compressed image set exceeding total decoded limits before retaining copies; cover transforms and alpha intermediates.\n- Render repeated references with a small decoded-byte budget and verify a typed refusal before large allocations.\n- Confirm repeated references share decoded storage and per-image limits remain effective.\n- Repeated references to one image must share immutable pixels and remain within an explicit aggregate decoded-byte budget."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:40a6bab8c3c48dfa6678571eff99a6238f11467771c1b52f0ead0a4a37581409"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Missing aggregate decoded-media resource budget",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_6aa9a8626de9bc707c34e4d3",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_dd507a63801cfb488fd8c71e",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "unbounded-allocation.decoded-image-references",
          "ruleIndex": 56
        },
