          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Identical duplicate relationship repair performs quadratic scans\n\nA relationship part with K distinct IDs followed by an identical second copy of each causes K(K-1)/2 membership comparisons in drop_repeated_relationships. For K=50,000 this is about 1.25 billion comparisons, despite fitting the configured XML part budget. Public PartFs opening performs this repair automatically.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Algorithmic complexity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-407\n\nRemediation:\nTrack repaired membership with a HashSet or a flag in the existing seen map, retaining the Vec solely for deterministic output order.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Many distinct identical duplicates repair with linear membership work.\n- Conflicting duplicates still refuse and deterministic repaired-ID reporting is unchanged."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:da339243aef52ff4c82f7da2fe28457b900313bac95cb3b02951b8c178d1bc4d"
          },
