          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Untrusted Markdown reference documents reach unchecked recursive XML parsing\n\nMarkdown conversion opens a caller-supplied reference DOCX using byte-only package bounds and parses its main XML without the XML-depth admission gate. A deeply nested reference can terminate the host processing it. The reference main part reaches section extraction irrespective of whether its body text is retained; Rust/Python/WASM and CLI reference paths share the boundary. Earlier low and assigned medium severity assessments are retained with their explicit untrusted-template prerequisite.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nAdmit every supplied reference DOCX under explicit active InputLimits before metadata, style, scholar, frame or other reference XML consumers parse it, or consistently use checked parsing at every main and preserved auxiliary XML boundary. Propagate limits and typed refusals across Rust/Python/WASM/CLI paths.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- An ordinary named reference main part with excessive nesting must return INVALID_XML before DOM construction.\n- Exercise Rust, Python, WASM and CLI reference-byte paths, plus valid trusted-template conversions.\n- Pass a structurally valid ZIP reference whose main XML exceeds depth 256 through Rust/Python/WASM imports and assert typed refusal before DOM construction.\n- Verify valid reference styles/page setup are preserved and raised explicit limits propagate consistently.\n- Pass a deeply nested main XML reference and assert INVALID_XML refusal before frame parsing.\n- Keep an ordinary bounded reference's page setup/styles behavior unchanged.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Bound the actual representation depth and processing work at the consuming boundary."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:0c9cc438628eb1b7a9c3d645d0c14e114d18d5de572c9c9b38d97093803749c1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "XML admission bypass / uncontrolled recursion",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_a69309b0b64d1048c5a4e319",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_dfc58569a3950cd270ca11bd",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "xml-admission-bypass.reference-document",
          "ruleIndex": 78
        },
