          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Rendering embedded HTML tables can expand a tiny colspan into billions of XML elements\n\nA DOCX containing an HTML/MHT altChunk can pass normal admission and then expand a short attacker-controlled `colspan` into one WordprocessingML grid column per declared column. The HTML conversion loop has no span, output-byte or work budget.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded generated output\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nBound HTML colspan and aggregate table columns with checked arithmetic, and enforce generated-WML byte/work limits while expanding altChunks. Refuse oversized content with a structured resource error.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Test excessive colspan in both HTML and base64/quoted-printable MHT chunks through public conversion.\n- Test aggregate span overflow and generated-output budget refusal.\n- Keep ordinary merged HTML tables working."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:0c4177140faddbbed35a7a48e83938db989b55e949778ffd9ed75cd4d1db047e"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unbounded generated output",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_f2b8de5e6202ea345a0e0c02",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_e152a6ec9d1056bf54ac83c0",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.html-table-columns",
          "ruleIndex": 46
        },
