          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Scanning a document for retained text can overflow the stack\n\nPublic `scrub::leaks()` enforces ZIP byte budgets but directly parses ordinary XML parts without the admission depth/tag policy. Any nonempty search needle activates this unchecked XML scan even when the needle is absent from the malicious XML; an empty needle returns immediately. Normal edit input admission may block deep conventionally named input before its postcheck.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-674\n\nRemediation:\nValidate each XML part with active depth/tag limits before DOM construction, reporting policy failure as a leak-scan refusal, or use a bounded streaming scan. Preserve deliberate empty-needle behavior; for nonempty needles, XML policy or encoding failures must produce a fail-closed incomplete-scan diagnostic even when the searched text is absent. Prefer the existing checked XML parser and preserve the failing part's context.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Deep ordinary .xml content produces a named policy failure instead of recursive parsing.\n- Active limits apply to every XML part scanned.\n- Direct leaks call on deep ordinary XML returns a fail-closed diagnostic before recursive parsing.\n- Verify well-formed bounded XML still finds text/entities/split Word runs and empty needle semantics stay deliberate.\n- Assert deeply nested XML returns a bounded fail-closed finding rather than recursing.\n- Cover exact permitted depth and malformed auxiliary XML without certifying incomplete scans.\n- Integration test a deeply nested XML part in an otherwise small package; scanner returns a finding without process termination.\n- Verify active max_xml_depth is enforced and exact-boundary input still scans.\n- Keep unreadable-entry and decoded/split-text leak checks fail closed.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Make security-sensitive scanner entrypoints self-bounding rather than relying on unrelated callers' admission."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:1cda4cf06f9e43062a80a99d396191b8240e59b5b6e8e6e3a83a8d8650735d8e"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Uncontrolled resource consumption",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_eb4256ff45478e77c3906750",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_ea3eeff7f3ced4976b62474f",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "unchecked-privacy-xml-recursion",
          "ruleIndex": 69
        },
