          "message": {
            "text": "Recording a plan in a shared directory can overwrite a symlink target\n\nThe Python and npm CLIs record edit/add plans through a predictable .<plan>.<pid>.partial file opened with ordinary truncating writes. A local attacker who can create entries in that directory can preplant the staging name as a symlink, causing valid plan JSON to overwrite another file writable by the victim before the rename.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Insecure temporary file\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-377\n\nRemediation:\nUse exclusive unpredictable staging in the destination directory, retain the opened handle for writing, and rename only that owned regular file. Reuse the native publication implementation for Python where possible; use exclusive creation (wx) with equivalent symlink/race protection in Node.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- In integration tests, preplant the historical predictable partial path as a symlink and verify its referent remains unchanged.\n- Exercise Python and npm plan recording with colliding staging names and failed writes; ensure cleanup only removes files created by the operation."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:7ce7caf5ee90b9b4139b315c7f3cc3475f5ef596c5650319ab12aa2645951cf5"
