          "message": {
            "text": "Chicago numbering expands one counter into a multi-gigabyte label\n\nA DOCX numbering level with numFmt=chicago, lvlText=%1 and start=4294967295 requests 1,073,741,824 copies of the three-byte marker \u2021 (3,221,225,472 bytes) before later copies/shaping. Both Markdown reading and PDF/PNG layout use the same formatter.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded generated allocation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nBound generated label length before repetition and apply a safe supported Chicago counter range or bounded fallback consistently across Markdown and layout.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A Chicago start=u32::MAX returns a bounded result or typed refusal before allocation.\n- Normal Chicago marker cycles and renderer/Markdown parity remain correct."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:6791fdccf4946a4cdc799e772127c6980bb64ed8eaec941f286170cc8b236934"
