          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "DOCX table spans drive attacker-sized column allocations\n\nRendering an admitted DOCX with one gridSpan=2147483647 cell requests roughly 8 GiB of f32 column storage before later layout. gridBefore/gridAfter reach the same occupancy calculation. A tiny numeric attribute bypasses byte-oriented resource budgets and can exhaust or terminate the host.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Unbounded allocation from table dimensions\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-789\n\nRemediation:\nEnforce maximum individual spans and total table columns before construction. Sum with checked arithmetic and return a typed resource refusal instead of allocating attacker-sized vectors. Apply the same bound to row skips.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A one-cell gridSpan=2147483647 package returns a normal refusal before layout.\n- Large gridBefore/gridAfter and overflowing span sums are refused; ordinary boundary spans still render."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:6ba380b08619a0cc5085c1de321150e7c6f76dcd34865dc04b5025f1f9285a4f"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Unbounded allocation from table dimensions",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_2ece2f7902f77a603a8c3e7d",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_f78cfb9da4af2b133ec903c5",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.table-grid-span",
          "ruleIndex": 51
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
