          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Markdown XML tree duplicates inherited namespace maps for each child declaration\n\nA root with 64 namespace bindings of 4,000-byte URIs followed by 20,000 empty children each declaring a small namespace forces the Markdown XML tree to retain roughly 5 GiB of copied inherited URI strings. This shallow source can stay below 1 MiB and within the active declaration, depth and attribute limits.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Namespace memory amplification\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-770\n\nRemediation:\nUse scope overlays or persistent maps storing shared URI values, and account retained namespace storage before allocation. Avoid cloning inherited String maps for every child declaration.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- A bounded regression for the identified input returns a normal refusal or bounded result before large allocation/recursion.\n- Ordinary documents at the active boundary continue to parse under caller-selected limits."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:699ff6bf2faa24c0819902e5e0116a3c2b20b00a32bb34e673ece25a98cb8663"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Namespace memory amplification",
