            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Algorithmic complexity: Relationship repair. Categories: Algorithmic complexity, Algorithmic complexity denial of service. Weaknesses: CWE-407."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Algorithmic complexity: Relationship repair. Categories: Algorithmic complexity, Algorithmic complexity denial of service. Weaknesses: CWE-407.\n\n## Remediation\n\nTrack already-reported duplicate IDs in a HashSet or alongside seen-map state, retaining a Vec only for deterministic reporting order. Optionally cap relationship-record/work totals before repair; test many distinct identical duplicate pairs while preserving deterministic repaired-ID order and conflicting-duplicate refusals.\n\nTrack already-reported duplicate IDs in a HashSet or alongside seen-map state, retaining a Vec only for deterministic reporting order. Optionally cap relationship-record/work totals before repair; test many distinct identical duplicate pairs while preserving deterministic repaired-ID order and conflicting-duplicate refusals. Apply an active relationship-record/work budget at metadata admission in addition to making duplicate membership near-linear.\n\nTrack repaired membership with a HashSet or a flag in the existing seen map, retaining the Vec solely for deterministic output order.",
                "text": "Algorithmic complexity: Relationship repair. Categories: Algorithmic complexity, Algorithmic complexity denial of service. Weaknesses: CWE-407.\n\nRemediation:\n\nTrack already-reported duplicate IDs in a HashSet or alongside seen-map state, retaining a Vec only for deterministic reporting order. Optionally cap relationship-record/work totals before repair; test many distinct identical duplicate pairs while preserving deterministic repaired-ID order and conflicting-duplicate refusals.\n\nTrack already-reported duplicate IDs in a HashSet or alongside seen-map state, retaining a Vec only for deterministic reporting order. Optionally cap relationship-record/work totals before repair; test many distinct identical duplicate pairs while preserving deterministic repaired-ID order and conflicting-duplicate refusals. Apply an active relationship-record/work budget at metadata admission in addition to making duplicate membership near-linear.\n\nTrack repaired membership with a HashSet or a flag in the existing seen map, retaining the Vec solely for deterministic output order."
              },
              "id": "algorithmic-complexity.relationship-repair",
