            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Ci: Untrusted code self hosted runner. Categories: CI isolation of untrusted code, CI isolation of untrusted code Untrusted code execution across a CI infrastructure boundary. Weaknesses: CWE-250, CWE-829."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Ci: Untrusted code self hosted runner. Categories: CI isolation of untrusted code, CI isolation of untrusted code Untrusted code execution across a CI infrastructure boundary. Weaknesses: CWE-250, CWE-829.\n\n## Remediation\n\nRun lower-trust PR builds/tests/generators on GitHub-hosted or one-job disposable runners without trusted writable state or private infrastructure connectivity. Separate trusted main runners and enforce cache write authorization server-side. Apply consistently to ci, adoption, docs and md-roundtrip.\n\nRun lower-trust PR builds/tests/generators on GitHub-hosted or one-job disposable runners without trusted writable state or private infrastructure connectivity. Separate trusted main runners and enforce cache write authorization server-side. Apply consistently to ci, adoption, docs and md-roundtrip.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Run untrusted PR jobs on GitHub-hosted or disposable isolated workers without trusted persistent stores/private services. Gate access to the shared self-hosted pool using trusted workflow logic outside PR control. Enforce cache read-only access at the service boundary when PRs need it.",
                "text": "Ci: Untrusted code self hosted runner. Categories: CI isolation of untrusted code, CI isolation of untrusted code Untrusted code execution across a CI infrastructure boundary. Weaknesses: CWE-250, CWE-829.\n\nRemediation:\n\nRun lower-trust PR builds/tests/generators on GitHub-hosted or one-job disposable runners without trusted writable state or private infrastructure connectivity. Separate trusted main runners and enforce cache write authorization server-side. Apply consistently to ci, adoption, docs and md-roundtrip.\n\nRun lower-trust PR builds/tests/generators on GitHub-hosted or one-job disposable runners without trusted writable state or private infrastructure connectivity. Separate trusted main runners and enforce cache write authorization server-side. Apply consistently to ci, adoption, docs and md-roundtrip.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Run untrusted PR jobs on GitHub-hosted or disposable isolated workers without trusted persistent stores/private services. Gate access to the shared self-hosted pool using trusted workflow logic outside PR control. Enforce cache read-only access at the service boundary when PRs need it."
              },
              "id": "ci.untrusted-code-self-hosted-runner",
              "name": "Ci: Untrusted code self hosted runner",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "CI isolation of untrusted code",
                  "CI isolation of untrusted code\nUntrusted code execution across a CI infrastructure boundary",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-250",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-829",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Ci: Untrusted code self hosted runner"
              }
            },
            {
