                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Legacy edit anchor search complexity"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Metadata scrub: Relationship targets. Categories: Incomplete removal of sensitive document metadata Incomplete removal of sensitive metadata Incomplete privacy sanitization Incomplete metadata selection for privacy removal. Weaknesses: CWE-200, CWE-201, CWE-212."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Metadata scrub: Relationship targets. Categories: Incomplete removal of sensitive document metadata Incomplete removal of sensitive metadata Incomplete privacy sanitization Incomplete metadata selection for privacy removal. Weaknesses: CWE-200, CWE-201, CWE-212.\n\n## Remediation\n\nResolve all core, extended and custom property parts through authoritative package relationships and content types, sanitize every applicable internal target according to docprops selection, and remove corresponding custom-property parts/relationships/content-type records coherently. Verify the selected privacy postcondition; refuse unsupported or ambiguous layouts rather than returning a successfully scrubbed copy. Preserve intentional title/subject/application and revision-date retention. Missing/invalid selected targets require explicit refusal or documented safe handling; default public and CLI callers must enforce the same postcondition. Include supported Strict property relationship variants and regression cases containing both conventional and relocated targets; every active property target must satisfy the requested postcondition.",
                "text": "Metadata scrub: Relationship targets. Categories: Incomplete removal of sensitive document metadata Incomplete removal of sensitive metadata Incomplete privacy sanitization Incomplete metadata selection for privacy removal. Weaknesses: CWE-200, CWE-201, CWE-212.\n\nRemediation:\n\nResolve all core, extended and custom property parts through authoritative package relationships and content types, sanitize every applicable internal target according to docprops selection, and remove corresponding custom-property parts/relationships/content-type records coherently. Verify the selected privacy postcondition; refuse unsupported or ambiguous layouts rather than returning a successfully scrubbed copy. Preserve intentional title/subject/application and revision-date retention. Missing/invalid selected targets require explicit refusal or documented safe handling; default public and CLI callers must enforce the same postcondition. Include supported Strict property relationship variants and regression cases containing both conventional and relocated targets; every active property target must satisfy the requested postcondition."
              },
              "id": "metadata-scrub.relationship-targets",
              "name": "Metadata scrub: Relationship targets",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Incomplete removal of sensitive document metadata\nIncomplete removal of sensitive metadata\nIncomplete privacy sanitization\nIncomplete metadata selection for privacy removal",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-200",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-201",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-212",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Metadata scrub: Relationship targets"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Metadata scrubbing: Utf16 XML. Categories: Incomplete metadata removal after XML decoding failure. Weaknesses: CWE-201."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Metadata scrubbing: Utf16 XML. Categories: Incomplete metadata removal after XML decoding failure. Weaknesses: CWE-201.\n\n## Remediation\n\nUse a shared encoding-aware XML decoder for selected metadata parts, and fail closed when a selected part cannot be parsed or requested identifying values remain. Handle both UTF-16 endiannesses consistently with admission.",
                "text": "Metadata scrubbing: Utf16 XML. Categories: Incomplete metadata removal after XML decoding failure. Weaknesses: CWE-201.\n\nRemediation:\n\nUse a shared encoding-aware XML decoder for selected metadata parts, and fail closed when a selected part cannot be parsed or requested identifying values remain. Handle both UTF-16 endiannesses consistently with admission."
              },
