            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Redaction: Utf16 XML retention. Categories: Incomplete removal of sensitive document information Incomplete sensitive data removal verification. Weaknesses: CWE-176, CWE-200, CWE-201, CWE-212."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Redaction: Utf16 XML retention. Categories: Incomplete removal of sensitive document information Incomplete sensitive data removal verification. Weaknesses: CWE-176, CWE-200, CWE-201, CWE-212.\n\n## Remediation\n\nDecode every XML part with the same BOM-aware policy as admission before semantic leak scanning. Fail closed on unsupported/undecodable/unparseable representations and retain raw UTF8 and both UTF16 byte-order checks as defense in depth. Use the same decoding across leak checks and package validation.",
                "text": "Redaction: Utf16 XML retention. Categories: Incomplete removal of sensitive document information Incomplete sensitive data removal verification. Weaknesses: CWE-176, CWE-200, CWE-201, CWE-212.\n\nRemediation:\n\nDecode every XML part with the same BOM-aware policy as admission before semantic leak scanning. Fail closed on unsupported/undecodable/unparseable representations and retain raw UTF8 and both UTF16 byte-order checks as defense in depth. Use the same decoding across leak checks and package validation."
              },
              "id": "redaction.utf16-xml-retention",
              "name": "Redaction: Utf16 XML retention",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Incomplete removal of sensitive document information\nIncomplete sensitive-data removal verification",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-176",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-200",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-201",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-212",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Redaction: Utf16 XML retention"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Redaction: XML encoding. Categories: Incomplete sensitive data redaction. Weaknesses: CWE-200."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Redaction: XML encoding. Categories: Incomplete sensitive data redaction. Weaknesses: CWE-200.\n\n## Remediation\n\nShare the XML decoder used by admission with the leak scanner, decode UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE before xml_holds, and refuse unrecognized/invalid encodings rather than silently classifying them as clean. Preserve raw-byte checks as defense in depth. Add redaction tests proving a UTF-16 customXml duplicate causes REDACTION_LEAK and no artifact is returned.",
                "text": "Redaction: XML encoding. Categories: Incomplete sensitive data redaction. Weaknesses: CWE-200.\n\nRemediation:\n\nShare the XML decoder used by admission with the leak scanner, decode UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE before xml_holds, and refuse unrecognized/invalid encodings rather than silently classifying them as clean. Preserve raw-byte checks as defense in depth. Add redaction tests proving a UTF-16 customXml duplicate causes REDACTION_LEAK and no artifact is returned."
              },
              "id": "redaction.xml-encoding",
              "name": "Redaction: XML encoding",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Incomplete sensitive-data redaction",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-200",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Redaction: XML encoding"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource amplification: Embedded font aliases. Categories: Unbounded expansion of shared embedded resources. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-409, CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource amplification: Embedded font aliases. Categories: Unbounded expansion of shared embedded resources. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-409, CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nCache decoded font buffers by resolved package part and effective obfuscation key, share Arc values across aliases, and enforce an aggregate decoded-font allocation/work budget before copying.\nEnforce face-count limits before decoding/retention and load only used faces where possible; cover all four style slots and different effective keys.",
                "text": "Resource amplification: Embedded font aliases. Categories: Unbounded expansion of shared embedded resources. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-409, CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nCache decoded font buffers by resolved package part and effective obfuscation key, share Arc values across aliases, and enforce an aggregate decoded-font allocation/work budget before copying.\nEnforce face-count limits before decoding/retention and load only used faces where possible; cover all four style slots and different effective keys."
              },
              "id": "resource-amplification.embedded-font-aliases",
              "name": "Resource amplification: Embedded font aliases",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Unbounded expansion of shared embedded resources",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-409",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-789",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource amplification: Embedded font aliases"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource amplification: Repeated altchunk. Categories: Unbounded post admission document expansion Unbounded logical document expansion. Weaknesses: CWE-409, CWE-770."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource amplification: Repeated altchunk. Categories: Unbounded post admission document expansion Unbounded logical document expansion. Weaknesses: CWE-409, CWE-770.\n\n## Remediation\n\nMake altChunk expansion fallible under active cumulative expanded-byte, node/element, depth, work and occurrence budgets. Check contributions before conversion/allocation/append, including repeated internal relationships and MIME-decoded chunks, and validate generated XML under active limits before DOM construction. Caching may reduce repeated conversion CPU but cannot replace the total-output budget.",
                "text": "Resource amplification: Repeated altchunk. Categories: Unbounded post admission document expansion Unbounded logical document expansion. Weaknesses: CWE-409, CWE-770.\n\nRemediation:\n\nMake altChunk expansion fallible under active cumulative expanded-byte, node/element, depth, work and occurrence budgets. Check contributions before conversion/allocation/append, including repeated internal relationships and MIME-decoded chunks, and validate generated XML under active limits before DOM construction. Caching may reduce repeated conversion CPU but cannot replace the total-output budget."
              },
              "id": "resource-amplification.repeated-altchunk",
              "name": "Resource amplification: Repeated altchunk",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Unbounded post-admission document expansion\nUnbounded logical document expansion",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-409",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-770",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource amplification: Repeated altchunk"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource amplification: Wmf record payload. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption Malformed record length permits overlapping allocation amplification Missing record local length validation. Weaknesses: CWE-1284, CWE-130, CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-770."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource amplification: Wmf record payload. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption Malformed record length permits overlapping allocation amplification Missing record local length validation. Weaknesses: CWE-1284, CWE-130, CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-770.\n\n## Remediation\n\nConfine every WMF handler, including field, font, string and geometry reads, to a slice limited to its checked declared record extent. Before allocation validate fixed fields, ring/point counts and coordinate arrays, EXTTEXTOUT options/optional rectangle and text count, and TEXTOUT padded string plus trailing coordinates against that slice using checked arithmetic. Refuse inconsistent records before decoding/rasterization/replay and enforce cumulative decoded-text, record and total geometry/work budgets. Keep the already bounded EMF behavior.",
                "text": "Resource amplification: Wmf record payload. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption Malformed record length permits overlapping allocation amplification Missing record local length validation. Weaknesses: CWE-1284, CWE-130, CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-770.\n\nRemediation:\n\nConfine every WMF handler, including field, font, string and geometry reads, to a slice limited to its checked declared record extent. Before allocation validate fixed fields, ring/point counts and coordinate arrays, EXTTEXTOUT options/optional rectangle and text count, and TEXTOUT padded string plus trailing coordinates against that slice using checked arithmetic. Refuse inconsistent records before decoding/rasterization/replay and enforce cumulative decoded-text, record and total geometry/work budgets. Keep the already bounded EMF behavior."
              },
              "id": "resource-amplification.wmf-record-payload",
              "name": "Resource amplification: Wmf record payload",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Uncontrolled resource consumption\nMalformed record length permits overlapping allocation amplification\nMissing record-local length validation",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-020",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-1284",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-130",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-770",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource amplification: Wmf record payload"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Altchunk colspan. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption. Weaknesses: CWE-400."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: Altchunk colspan. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption. Weaknesses: CWE-400.\n\n## Remediation\n\nReject or cap colspan before storing it, use checked totals, and enforce a total generated grid/output budget before expanding HTML/MHT chunks. Return a typed conversion refusal for oversized tables.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Altchunk colspan. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption. Weaknesses: CWE-400.\n\nRemediation:\n\nReject or cap colspan before storing it, use checked totals, and enforce a total generated grid/output budget before expanding HTML/MHT chunks. Return a typed conversion refusal for oversized tables."
              },
              "id": "resource-exhaustion.altchunk-colspan",
              "name": "Resource exhaustion: Altchunk colspan",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Uncontrolled resource consumption",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Altchunk colspan"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago number label. Categories: Unbounded generated string allocation, Uncontrolled allocation in numeric label expansion Unbounded allocation in number label formatting. Weaknesses: CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago number label. Categories: Unbounded generated string allocation, Uncontrolled allocation in numeric label expansion Unbounded allocation in number label formatting. Weaknesses: CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nBound generated byte/glyph length inside the shared Chicago formatter before repetition, with a documented safe cycle/fallback or typed refusal. Apply that bound to all list, startOverride, section-page and Markdown/direct list_number callers; do not rely on input bytes, counter saturation or later clipping. Include authored endnote numStart/format and MCP agent-view callers in the shared formatter budget.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Apply a central maximum output length to Chicago labels before repetition and enforce a cumulative numbering-output budget. Use a documented bounded fallback or typed refusal consistently for list, read/agent, page and future formatter consumers.\n\nEnforce a maximum generated label length before symbol repetition and return a typed resource refusal or bounded documented fallback. Reuse the guard for every Chicago formatter consumer, including list, page and note numbering.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago number label. Categories: Unbounded generated string allocation, Uncontrolled allocation in numeric label expansion Unbounded allocation in number label formatting. Weaknesses: CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nBound generated byte/glyph length inside the shared Chicago formatter before repetition, with a documented safe cycle/fallback or typed refusal. Apply that bound to all list, startOverride, section-page and Markdown/direct list_number callers; do not rely on input bytes, counter saturation or later clipping. Include authored endnote numStart/format and MCP agent-view callers in the shared formatter budget.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Apply a central maximum output length to Chicago labels before repetition and enforce a cumulative numbering-output budget. Use a documented bounded fallback or typed refusal consistently for list, read/agent, page and future formatter consumers.\n\nEnforce a maximum generated label length before symbol repetition and return a typed resource refusal or bounded documented fallback. Reuse the guard for every Chicago formatter consumer, including list, page and note numbering."
              },
              "id": "resource-exhaustion.chicago-number-label",
              "name": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago number label",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Unbounded generated string allocation",
                  "Uncontrolled allocation in numeric label expansion\nUnbounded allocation in number-label formatting",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-789",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago number label"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago numbering. Categories: Unbounded generated allocation. Weaknesses: CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago numbering. Categories: Unbounded generated allocation. Weaknesses: CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nBound generated label length before repetition and apply a safe supported Chicago counter range or bounded fallback consistently across Markdown and layout.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Chicago numbering. Categories: Unbounded generated allocation. Weaknesses: CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nBound generated label length before repetition and apply a safe supported Chicago counter range or bounded fallback consistently across Markdown and layout."
              },
