            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level. Categories: Excessive iteration from numbering metadata. Weaknesses: CWE-834."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level. Categories: Excessive iteration from numbering metadata. Weaknesses: CWE-834.\n\n## Remediation\n\nValidate paragraph, style, abstract-level and override ilvl values against supported numbering levels before use. Find a parent by examining declared keys and avoid populating nonexistent levels. Return a normal refusal for unsupported values.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level. Categories: Excessive iteration from numbering metadata. Weaknesses: CWE-834.\n\nRemediation:\n\nValidate paragraph, style, abstract-level and override ilvl values against supported numbering levels before use. Find a parent by examining declared keys and avoid populating nonexistent levels. Return a normal refusal for unsupported values."
              },
              "id": "resource-exhaustion.numbering-level",
              "name": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Excessive iteration from numbering metadata",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-834",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level range. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption Unchecked input controlling loop bounds. Weaknesses: CWE-606, CWE-834."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level range. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption Unchecked input controlling loop bounds. Weaknesses: CWE-606, CWE-834.\n\n## Remediation\n\nValidate the supported ilvl domain in paragraph, style, abstract and override sources before use. Find fallback levels among actual defined keys and initialize/substitute only supported or defined levels; avoid any iteration or allocation proportional to an untrusted numeric level. Return a typed refusal for unsupported level metadata rather than attempting dense counter or placeholder materialization.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Validate paragraph and numbering-definition level IDs against the supported 0..=8 range. Resolve ancestors by actual defined keys and bound synthesized counters and marker iteration independently of untrusted integer values.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level range. Categories: Uncontrolled resource consumption Unchecked input controlling loop bounds. Weaknesses: CWE-606, CWE-834.\n\nRemediation:\n\nValidate the supported ilvl domain in paragraph, style, abstract and override sources before use. Find fallback levels among actual defined keys and initialize/substitute only supported or defined levels; avoid any iteration or allocation proportional to an untrusted numeric level. Return a typed refusal for unsupported level metadata rather than attempting dense counter or placeholder materialization.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Validate paragraph and numbering-definition level IDs against the supported 0..=8 range. Resolve ancestors by actual defined keys and bound synthesized counters and marker iteration independently of untrusted integer values."
              },
              "id": "resource-exhaustion.numbering-level-range",
              "name": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level range",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Uncontrolled resource consumption\nUnchecked input controlling loop bounds",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-606",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-834",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Numbering level range"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Table grid span. Categories: Unbounded allocation from table dimensions, Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions, Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions Unbounded allocation from document table metadata. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: Table grid span. Categories: Unbounded allocation from table dimensions, Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions, Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions Unbounded allocation from document table metadata. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nBound HTML table column counts with checked sums and cap generated altChunk WML bytes during emission. Propagate a typed refusal to the renderer before expansion or parsing.\n\nEnforce maximum individual spans and total table columns before construction. Sum with checked arithmetic and return a typed resource refusal instead of allocating attacker-sized vectors. Apply the same bound to row skips.\n\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess.\n\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess. Propagate a caller-adjustable semantic column limit through all public rendering surfaces and charge later column/merge vectors to that same budget.\n\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess. Propagate a caller-adjustable semantic column limit through all public rendering surfaces and charge later column/merge vectors to that same budget.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Enforce explicit maximum live cell spans, row skips, aggregate table columns and merge slots before any allocation. Use checked sums and a cumulative layout resource budget, returning a typed refusal when exceeded.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Table grid span. Categories: Unbounded allocation from table dimensions, Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions, Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans Unbounded allocation from document dimensions Unbounded allocation from document table metadata. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nBound HTML table column counts with checked sums and cap generated altChunk WML bytes during emission. Propagate a typed refusal to the renderer before expansion or parsing.\n\nEnforce maximum individual spans and total table columns before construction. Sum with checked arithmetic and return a typed resource refusal instead of allocating attacker-sized vectors. Apply the same bound to row skips.\n\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess.\n\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess. Propagate a caller-adjustable semantic column limit through all public rendering surfaces and charge later column/merge vectors to that same budget.\n\nEnforce practical per-span and total-column budgets for gridSpan, gridBefore and gridAfter before excessive RawCell, column, preference or merge allocation/work. Use checked occupancy sums and col+span arithmetic, apply the same budget to every derived table vector, and return a typed resource-limit refusal on excess. Propagate a caller-adjustable semantic column limit through all public rendering surfaces and charge later column/merge vectors to that same budget.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Enforce explicit maximum live cell spans, row skips, aggregate table columns and merge slots before any allocation. Use checked sums and a cumulative layout resource budget, returning a typed refusal when exceeded."
              },
              "id": "resource-exhaustion.table-grid-span",
              "name": "Resource exhaustion: Table grid span",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Unbounded allocation from table dimensions",
                  "Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans\nUnbounded allocation from document dimensions",
                  "Uncontrolled memory allocation from table spans\nUnbounded allocation from document dimensions\nUnbounded allocation from document table metadata",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-789",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: Table grid span"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: XML namespace interning. Categories: Namespace memory amplification. Weaknesses: CWE-770."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Resource exhaustion: XML namespace interning. Categories: Namespace memory amplification. Weaknesses: CWE-770.\n\n## Remediation\n\nShare active namespace URI allocations directly from parser scope independently of global-pool capacity, or use bounded per-document interning with explicit refusal when storage budget is exhausted.",
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: XML namespace interning. Categories: Namespace memory amplification. Weaknesses: CWE-770.\n\nRemediation:\n\nShare active namespace URI allocations directly from parser scope independently of global-pool capacity, or use bounded per-document interning with explicit refusal when storage budget is exhausted."
              },
              "id": "resource-exhaustion.xml-namespace-interning",
              "name": "Resource exhaustion: XML namespace interning",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Namespace memory amplification",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-770",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource exhaustion: XML namespace interning"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Symlink following: Font index staging. Categories: Symlink following in font cache publication. Weaknesses: CWE-377, CWE-59, CWE-61."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Symlink following: Font index staging. Categories: Symlink following in font cache publication. Weaknesses: CWE-377, CWE-59, CWE-61.\n\n## Remediation\n\nPublish the font index through an unpredictable private staging directory and an exclusively created regular file held open through writing. Atomically rename only that file; refuse preexisting staging entries and document/private-parent expectations for shared configurations.",
                "text": "Symlink following: Font index staging. Categories: Symlink following in font cache publication. Weaknesses: CWE-377, CWE-59, CWE-61.\n\nRemediation:\n\nPublish the font index through an unpredictable private staging directory and an exclusively created regular file held open through writing. Atomically rename only that file; refuse preexisting staging entries and document/private-parent expectations for shared configurations."
              },
              "id": "symlink-following.font-index-staging",
              "name": "Symlink following: Font index staging",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Symlink following in font-cache publication",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-059",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-061",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-377",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Symlink following: Font index staging"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Symlink following: Plan staging. Categories: Symlink following in temporary file creation, Symlink following in temporary file publication. Weaknesses: CWE-377, CWE-59, CWE-61."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Symlink following: Plan staging. Categories: Symlink following in temporary file creation, Symlink following in temporary file publication. Weaknesses: CWE-377, CWE-59, CWE-61.\n\n## Remediation\n\nCreate an unpredictable private staging directory next to the plan and open the staged regular file exclusively. Write through its held descriptor and rename only that file. At minimum refuse every preexisting staging entry using exclusive creation rather than default truncating writes.\n\nRoute Python recording through the existing native exclusive publication function. For npm, exclusively create a randomly named private staging directory/file in the plan parent, write and verify through a held descriptor, then atomically rename. Refuse existing staging names and avoid following links. Apply exclusive private staging to FontIndex::save as well, and keep shared cache storage segregated by OS principal.",
                "text": "Symlink following: Plan staging. Categories: Symlink following in temporary file creation, Symlink following in temporary file publication. Weaknesses: CWE-377, CWE-59, CWE-61.\n\nRemediation:\n\nCreate an unpredictable private staging directory next to the plan and open the staged regular file exclusively. Write through its held descriptor and rename only that file. At minimum refuse every preexisting staging entry using exclusive creation rather than default truncating writes.\n\nRoute Python recording through the existing native exclusive publication function. For npm, exclusively create a randomly named private staging directory/file in the plan parent, write and verify through a held descriptor, then atomically rename. Refuse existing staging names and avoid following links. Apply exclusive private staging to FontIndex::save as well, and keep shared cache storage segregated by OS principal."
              },
              "id": "symlink-following.plan-staging",
              "name": "Symlink following: Plan staging",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Symlink following in temporary file creation",
                  "Symlink following in temporary-file publication",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-059",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-061",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-377",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Symlink following: Plan staging"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Css selector groups. Categories: Uncontrolled memory allocation. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Unbounded allocation: Css selector groups. Categories: Uncontrolled memory allocation. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nShare immutable declaration maps/values across grouped selectors and enforce cumulative selector, rule and declaration-byte budgets before allocation. Enforce value-length limits and discard unsupported properties before retaining them; unused selectors and properties must still count toward the aggregate budget.",
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Css selector groups. Categories: Uncontrolled memory allocation. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nShare immutable declaration maps/values across grouped selectors and enforce cumulative selector, rule and declaration-byte budgets before allocation. Enforce value-length limits and discard unsupported properties before retaining them; unused selectors and properties must still count toward the aggregate budget."
              },
              "id": "unbounded-allocation.css-selector-groups",
              "name": "Unbounded allocation: Css selector groups",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Uncontrolled memory allocation",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-789",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Css selector groups"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Decoded image references. Categories: Missing aggregate decoded media resource budget. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-770."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Unbounded allocation: Decoded image references. Categories: Missing aggregate decoded media resource budget. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-770.\n\n## Remediation\n\nApply a conversion-wide decoded-pixel/byte budget before decoding or retaining media, cache decoded parts by source and transformation, and use shared immutable samples in layout/display operations. Count transformed and temporary buffers against the same budget. Apply the same sharing and aggregate accounting to group-picture, VML-preview and picture-bullet consumers, keyed by effective transformation; retain all earlier display-list/temporary-buffer accounting.",
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Decoded image references. Categories: Missing aggregate decoded media resource budget. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-770.\n\nRemediation:\n\nApply a conversion-wide decoded-pixel/byte budget before decoding or retaining media, cache decoded parts by source and transformation, and use shared immutable samples in layout/display operations. Count transformed and temporary buffers against the same budget. Apply the same sharing and aggregate accounting to group-picture, VML-preview and picture-bullet consumers, keyed by effective transformation; retain all earlier display-list/temporary-buffer accounting."
              },
              "id": "unbounded-allocation.decoded-image-references",
              "name": "Unbounded allocation: Decoded image references",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Missing aggregate decoded-media resource budget",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-770",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Decoded image references"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Legacy logical story. Categories: Memory allocation with excessive size value Unbounded decoded document expansion Unbounded logical text expansion, Memory allocation with excessive size value Unbounded decoded document expansion Unbounded logical text expansion Logical data amplification in legacy document decoding. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-409, CWE-770, CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Unbounded allocation: Legacy logical story. Categories: Memory allocation with excessive size value Unbounded decoded document expansion Unbounded logical text expansion, Memory allocation with excessive size value Unbounded decoded document expansion Unbounded logical text expansion Logical data amplification in legacy document decoding. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-409, CWE-770, CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nIntroduce configurable legacy physical-input, piece-count, cumulative logical-character, retained-metadata and expansion-work budgets. Check FIB ccp_text and checked cumulative piece lengths before materialization, charge every decoded character including repeated physical aliases, and return typed refusals through read/doc_to_markdown/doc_to_docx and CLI callers. Preserve legitimate fast-save aliases and split UTF-16 surrogate handling within budget.\n\nIntroduce configurable legacy physical-input, piece-count, cumulative logical-character, retained-metadata and expansion-work budgets. Check FIB ccp_text and checked cumulative piece lengths before materialization, charge every decoded character including repeated physical aliases, and return typed refusals through read/doc_to_markdown/doc_to_docx and CLI callers. Preserve legitimate fast-save aliases and split UTF-16 surrogate handling within budget. Replace full legacy parsing used only for diagnostic refusal hints with a cheap bounded probe, or apply the same logical/work budgets before that parser runs.\n\nIntroduce configurable legacy physical-input, piece-count, cumulative logical-character, retained-metadata and expansion-work budgets. Check FIB ccp_text and checked cumulative piece lengths before materialization, charge every decoded character including repeated physical aliases, and return typed refusals through read/doc_to_markdown/doc_to_docx and CLI callers. Preserve legitimate fast-save aliases and split UTF-16 surrogate handling within budget. Replace full legacy parsing used only for diagnostic refusal hints with a cheap bounded probe, or apply the same logical/work budgets before that parser runs.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Introduce a configurable legacy logical-character/output budget, check ccp_text and cumulative decoded piece work before materialization, and enforce it during decoding. Preserve valid reuse while returning a typed refusal for excessive expansion.",
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Legacy logical story. Categories: Memory allocation with excessive size value Unbounded decoded document expansion Unbounded logical text expansion, Memory allocation with excessive size value Unbounded decoded document expansion Unbounded logical text expansion Logical data amplification in legacy document decoding. Weaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-409, CWE-770, CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nIntroduce configurable legacy physical-input, piece-count, cumulative logical-character, retained-metadata and expansion-work budgets. Check FIB ccp_text and checked cumulative piece lengths before materialization, charge every decoded character including repeated physical aliases, and return typed refusals through read/doc_to_markdown/doc_to_docx and CLI callers. Preserve legitimate fast-save aliases and split UTF-16 surrogate handling within budget.\n\nIntroduce configurable legacy physical-input, piece-count, cumulative logical-character, retained-metadata and expansion-work budgets. Check FIB ccp_text and checked cumulative piece lengths before materialization, charge every decoded character including repeated physical aliases, and return typed refusals through read/doc_to_markdown/doc_to_docx and CLI callers. Preserve legitimate fast-save aliases and split UTF-16 surrogate handling within budget. Replace full legacy parsing used only for diagnostic refusal hints with a cheap bounded probe, or apply the same logical/work budgets before that parser runs.\n\nIntroduce configurable legacy physical-input, piece-count, cumulative logical-character, retained-metadata and expansion-work budgets. Check FIB ccp_text and checked cumulative piece lengths before materialization, charge every decoded character including repeated physical aliases, and return typed refusals through read/doc_to_markdown/doc_to_docx and CLI callers. Preserve legitimate fast-save aliases and split UTF-16 surrogate handling within budget. Replace full legacy parsing used only for diagnostic refusal hints with a cheap bounded probe, or apply the same logical/work budgets before that parser runs.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Introduce a configurable legacy logical-character/output budget, check ccp_text and cumulative decoded piece work before materialization, and enforce it during decoding. Preserve valid reuse while returning a typed refusal for excessive expansion."
              },
              "id": "unbounded-allocation.legacy-logical-story",
              "name": "Unbounded allocation: Legacy logical story",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Memory allocation with excessive size value\nUnbounded decoded-document expansion\nUnbounded logical text expansion",
                  "Memory allocation with excessive size value\nUnbounded decoded-document expansion\nUnbounded logical text expansion\nLogical data amplification in legacy document decoding",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-409",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-770",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-789",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Legacy logical story"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Tab leader. Categories: Memory allocation with excessive size value. Weaknesses: CWE-789."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Unbounded allocation: Tab leader. Categories: Memory allocation with excessive size value. Weaknesses: CWE-789.\n\n## Remediation\n\nReject nonfinite coordinates and cap tab destinations or generated leader glyphs to the visible line/page extent before constructing strings.",
                "text": "Unbounded allocation: Tab leader. Categories: Memory allocation with excessive size value. Weaknesses: CWE-789.\n\nRemediation:\n\nReject nonfinite coordinates and cap tab destinations or generated leader glyphs to the visible line/page extent before constructing strings."
              },
