            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unsafe filesystem publication: Symlink following. Categories: Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following, Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following Time of check time of use output race. Weaknesses: CWE-367, CWE-61."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Unsafe filesystem publication: Symlink following. Categories: Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following, Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following Time of check time of use output race. Weaknesses: CWE-367, CWE-61.\n\n## Remediation\n\nPublish Python/Node ordinary outputs, bundles and reports through held-directory authority and exclusive private staging. Atomically install without replacement when --force is false, or atomically replace the authorized destination entry when true; never truncate through a mutable final pathname. Apply exclusive unpredictable regular-file staging beside the authorized target to Python plan recording. Node recordPlan staging retains its separately established repair and identity.\n\nPublish Python/Node ordinary outputs, bundles and reports through held-directory authority and exclusive private staging. Atomically install without replacement when --force is false, or atomically replace the authorized destination entry when true; never truncate through a mutable final pathname. Apply exclusive unpredictable regular-file staging beside the authorized target to Python plan recording. Node recordPlan staging retains its separately established repair and identity. Expose/reuse native publication for Python CLI outputs with overwrite authorization passed into the commit operation; Node host publication must provide equivalent exclusive staging and atomic no-clobber/replacement. Preserve the documented final-output rule: forced publication replaces the selected symlink directory entry itself and leaves its referent unchanged; no-force installation must refuse an already occupied destination, including a dangling symlink.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Use staged verified publication with held parent-directory authority for both wrappers. Carry overwrite authorization through commit and atomically refuse any existing destination when force is false; do not rely on a preliminary exists check.",
                "text": "Unsafe filesystem publication: Symlink following. Categories: Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following, Unsafe filesystem publication symbolic link following Time of check time of use output race. Weaknesses: CWE-367, CWE-61.\n\nRemediation:\n\nPublish Python/Node ordinary outputs, bundles and reports through held-directory authority and exclusive private staging. Atomically install without replacement when --force is false, or atomically replace the authorized destination entry when true; never truncate through a mutable final pathname. Apply exclusive unpredictable regular-file staging beside the authorized target to Python plan recording. Node recordPlan staging retains its separately established repair and identity.\n\nPublish Python/Node ordinary outputs, bundles and reports through held-directory authority and exclusive private staging. Atomically install without replacement when --force is false, or atomically replace the authorized destination entry when true; never truncate through a mutable final pathname. Apply exclusive unpredictable regular-file staging beside the authorized target to Python plan recording. Node recordPlan staging retains its separately established repair and identity. Expose/reuse native publication for Python CLI outputs with overwrite authorization passed into the commit operation; Node host publication must provide equivalent exclusive staging and atomic no-clobber/replacement. Preserve the documented final-output rule: forced publication replaces the selected symlink directory entry itself and leaves its referent unchanged; no-force installation must refuse an already occupied destination, including a dangling symlink.\nAdditional retained remediation detail: Use staged verified publication with held parent-directory authority for both wrappers. Carry overwrite authorization through commit and atomically refuse any existing destination when force is false; do not rely on a preliminary exists check."
              },
              "id": "unsafe-filesystem-publication.symlink-following",
              "name": "Unsafe filesystem publication: Symlink following",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Unsafe filesystem publication / symbolic link following",
                  "Unsafe filesystem publication / symbolic link following\nTime-of-check/time-of-use output race",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-061",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-367",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unsafe filesystem publication: Symlink following"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XML admission bypass: Reference document. Categories: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion. Weaknesses: CWE-674."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "XML admission bypass: Reference document. Categories: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\n## Remediation\n\nAdmit every supplied reference DOCX under explicit active InputLimits before metadata, style, scholar, frame or other reference XML consumers parse it, or consistently use checked parsing at every main and preserved auxiliary XML boundary. Propagate limits and typed refusals across Rust/Python/WASM/CLI paths.",
                "text": "XML admission bypass: Reference document. Categories: XML admission bypass uncontrolled recursion. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\nRemediation:\n\nAdmit every supplied reference DOCX under explicit active InputLimits before metadata, style, scholar, frame or other reference XML consumers parse it, or consistently use checked parsing at every main and preserved auxiliary XML boundary. Propagate limits and typed refusals across Rust/Python/WASM/CLI paths."
              },
              "id": "xml-admission-bypass.reference-document",
              "name": "XML admission bypass: Reference document",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "XML admission bypass / uncontrolled recursion",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-674",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "XML admission bypass: Reference document"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XML admission: Markdown reference. Categories: Unchecked XML recursion. Weaknesses: CWE-674."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "XML admission: Markdown reference. Categories: Unchecked XML recursion. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\n## Remediation\n\nAdmit options.reference before any reference inspection or assembly, return a typed reference refusal on failure, and use checked parsing when extracting section properties. Add a regression that supplies a normally named over-depth main document as reference through the Rust API and bindings.",
                "text": "XML admission: Markdown reference. Categories: Unchecked XML recursion. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\nRemediation:\n\nAdmit options.reference before any reference inspection or assembly, return a typed reference refusal on failure, and use checked parsing when extracting section properties. Add a regression that supplies a normally named over-depth main document as reference through the Rust API and bindings."
              },
              "id": "xml-admission.markdown-reference",
              "name": "XML admission: Markdown reference",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Unchecked XML recursion",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-674",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "XML admission: Markdown reference"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XML admission: Relationship target. Categories: XML resource limit bypass. Weaknesses: CWE-674."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "XML admission: Relationship target. Categories: XML resource limit bypass. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\n## Remediation\n\nBefore each renderer DOM construction, use try_parse_xdocument_with_limits with the active limits, or admit all relationship/content-type identified XML parts regardless of filename suffix. Add integration regressions for over-depth styles/theme parts named .bin and verify the ordinary INVALID_XML refusal on PDF and PNG paths.",
                "text": "XML admission: Relationship target. Categories: XML resource limit bypass. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\nRemediation:\n\nBefore each renderer DOM construction, use try_parse_xdocument_with_limits with the active limits, or admit all relationship/content-type identified XML parts regardless of filename suffix. Add integration regressions for over-depth styles/theme parts named .bin and verify the ordinary INVALID_XML refusal on PDF and PNG paths."
              },
              "id": "xml-admission.relationship-target",
              "name": "XML admission: Relationship target",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "XML resource-limit bypass",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-674",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "XML admission: Relationship target"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XML depth: Dtd parser differential. Categories: Uncontrolled recursion from XML parser disagreement XML grammar differential bypassing recursion policy XML admission parser differential. Weaknesses: CWE-674."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "XML depth: Dtd parser differential. Categories: Uncontrolled recursion from XML parser disagreement XML grammar differential bypassing recursion policy XML admission parser differential. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\n## Remediation\n\nAlign admission and DOM lexical/structural semantics for every opaque <! construct. Reject unsupported DTD and CDATA/text outside the root consistently with checked XML validation, and enforce active depth during DOM construction or use the checked API before every untrusted consumer. If opaque constructs are supported, consume their complete grammar rather than the first '>'. A DTD-only refusal does not fix the top-level CDATA subcase; retain valid in-root CDATA. Include get_revisions main-document parsing in the mandatory lexical/depth boundary while preserving existing checked-consumer distinctions.",
                "text": "XML depth: Dtd parser differential. Categories: Uncontrolled recursion from XML parser disagreement XML grammar differential bypassing recursion policy XML admission parser differential. Weaknesses: CWE-674.\n\nRemediation:\n\nAlign admission and DOM lexical/structural semantics for every opaque <! construct. Reject unsupported DTD and CDATA/text outside the root consistently with checked XML validation, and enforce active depth during DOM construction or use the checked API before every untrusted consumer. If opaque constructs are supported, consume their complete grammar rather than the first '>'. A DTD-only refusal does not fix the top-level CDATA subcase; retain valid in-root CDATA. Include get_revisions main-document parsing in the mandatory lexical/depth boundary while preserving existing checked-consumer distinctions."
              },
              "id": "xml-depth.dtd-parser-differential",
              "name": "XML depth: Dtd parser differential",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Uncontrolled recursion from XML parser disagreement\nXML grammar differential bypassing recursion policy\nXML admission/parser differential",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-674",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "XML depth: Dtd parser differential"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XML hash opening tag quadratic scan. Categories: Algorithmic complexity in XML hashing. Weaknesses: CWE-407."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "XML hash opening tag quadratic scan. Categories: Algorithmic complexity in XML hashing. Weaknesses: CWE-407.\n\n## Remediation\n\nSearch only the new fragment for the root-tag terminator or expose explicit tag-completion state from serialization. Preserve linear behavior for escaped values and test large retained custom attributes through public comparison.",
                "text": "XML hash opening tag quadratic scan. Categories: Algorithmic complexity in XML hashing. Weaknesses: CWE-407.\n\nRemediation:\n\nSearch only the new fragment for the root-tag terminator or expose explicit tag-completion state from serialization. Preserve linear behavior for escaped values and test large retained custom attributes through public comparison."
              },
