            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Zip entry budget: Eocd selection differential. Categories: Input validation ZIP parser differential ZIP metadata resource policy bypass. Weaknesses: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-770."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Zip entry budget: Eocd selection differential. Categories: Input validation ZIP parser differential ZIP metadata resource policy bypass. Weaknesses: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-770.\n\n## Remediation\n\nUse the delegated reader's authoritative validated EOCD/ZIP64 selection, consistent ZIP32 total/per-disk fields and all ZIP64 total/size/offset triggers. Bound raw central-record traversal/count before index allocation, reject inconsistent unsupported metadata, and retain a post-open active archive.len cap as defense in depth; that later check cannot undo earlier allocation. Reconcile selected raw counts with indexed counts for exact duplicates, including name collapse, comments, ZIP64 and prepended data. Detect raw exact-name duplicates directly or through the reader's duplicate flag rather than relying solely on a count-shortfall inference.",
                "text": "Zip entry budget: Eocd selection differential. Categories: Input validation ZIP parser differential ZIP metadata resource policy bypass. Weaknesses: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-770.\n\nRemediation:\n\nUse the delegated reader's authoritative validated EOCD/ZIP64 selection, consistent ZIP32 total/per-disk fields and all ZIP64 total/size/offset triggers. Bound raw central-record traversal/count before index allocation, reject inconsistent unsupported metadata, and retain a post-open active archive.len cap as defense in depth; that later check cannot undo earlier allocation. Reconcile selected raw counts with indexed counts for exact duplicates, including name collapse, comments, ZIP64 and prepended data. Detect raw exact-name duplicates directly or through the reader's duplicate flag rather than relying solely on a count-shortfall inference."
              },
              "id": "zip-entry-budget.eocd-selection-differential",
              "name": "Zip entry budget: Eocd selection differential",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "Input validation / ZIP parser differential\nZIP metadata resource-policy bypass",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-020",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-400",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-770",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Zip entry budget: Eocd selection differential"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Zip preindex budget bypass. Categories: Resource limits applied after expensive ZIP parsing. Weaknesses: CWE-400."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Zip preindex budget bypass. Categories: Resource limits applied after expensive ZIP parsing. Weaknesses: CWE-400.\n\n## Remediation\n\nApply a documented compressed-input and declared-entry preindex budget before opening metadata ZIPs,or enforce it centrally in Package::open. Preserve best-effort absent-metadata behavior only after a cheap bounded refusal.",
                "text": "Zip preindex budget bypass. Categories: Resource limits applied after expensive ZIP parsing. Weaknesses: CWE-400.\n\nRemediation:\n\nApply a documented compressed-input and declared-entry preindex budget before opening metadata ZIPs,or enforce it centrally in Package::open. Preserve best-effort absent-metadata behavior only after a cheap bounded refusal."
              },
              "id": "zip-preindex-budget-bypass",
